t["npc:coleman-farthing"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,371,16.546.0,24.507.0,36.109.0,49.315.0,35.254.0,44.239.0,51.293.0,47.134.0",["h"]="197399",["n"]="Coleman Lontananza",["s"]="Coleman Lontananza. Coleman Lontananza es un amargado superviviente Renegado que reside en el Mesón La Horca en Rémol. En vida, trabajó para la acaudalada dinastía Agamand en sus extensos molinos de harina en el norte de Tirisfal. Convencido para quedarse y defender la finca contra la Plaga, murió junto a sus compañeros de trabajo y ahora dedica su no-muerte a cobrarse venganza de sus antiguos amos. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, Coleman Lontananza se ganaba honradamente la vida como obrero en los Molinos de Agamand, la mayor explotación agrícola y harinera de los Claros de Tirisfal. Cuando la Plaga arrasó Lordaeron, la aristocrática familia Agamand se negó a huir de sus valiosas tierras. En su lugar, instaron a sus sirvientes y peones a tomar las armas junto a ellos, prometiendo que podrían defender las granjas contra la horda de no-muertos. Coleman y sus compañeros se quedaron, confiando en sus señores, una decisión que les costó la vida a todos y cada uno de ellos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Coleman points aspiring warriors directly toward the Agamand Family Crypt, urging them to plunder the martial heirlooms of a fallen aristocratic house to arm themselves for the wars ahead.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Coleman represents the shared resentment many commoners hold toward Lordaeron's old nobility, whose arrogance and pride often hastened their subjects' demise during the plague."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Coleman Farthing spends his days inside the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, located in central Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"coleman farthing location","where is coleman farthing","coleman farthing brill"},["q"]="Where can Coleman Farthing be found?"},{["a"]="When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the Agamand patriarchs convinced their workers—including Coleman—to stay and fight to protect the mills rather than flee to safety. The entire workforce was slaughtered as a result. Coleman views their rallying cry as arrogant manipulation that led him directly to his death.",["al"]={"why does coleman hate agamands","coleman farthing motivation","agamand mills grudge"},["q"]="Why does Coleman hate the Agamand family so much?"},{["a"]="The sprawling estate was completely overrun by the Scourge. Its wind-driven mills stand ruined and haunted, while the Agamand family members and their slaughtered workers wander the blighted fields as mindlessly hostile undead under the Lich King's sway.",["al"]={"what happened to agamand mills","agamand mills lore","who owns agamand mills"},["q"]="What happened to the Agamand Mills?"},{["a"]="Coleman directs adventurers to journey north to the Agamand Mills to cull the roaming undead, slay the risen members of the Agamand lineage to recover their remains for desecration, and raid the Agamand Family Crypt for ancestral weaponry.",["al"]={"coleman farthing quests","agamand quests brill"},["q"]="What tasks does Coleman give to adventurers?"},{["a"]="Coleman sees the Agamands' ancestral weaponry as symbols of the hollow pride that led his fellow workers to their deaths. He sends skilled warriors to plunder these relics from the family crypt, both to strip the dynasty of its honor and put the weapons to practical use against their enemies.",["al"]={"agamand heirlooms quest lore","why steal agamand weapons"},["q"]="Why does Coleman want the Agamand heirloom weapons?"},{["a"]="They share a surname and origins in the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, but there is no confirmed record of their specific familial ties.",["al"]={"bishop farthing relation","coleman farthing family"},["q"]="Is Coleman Farthing related to Bishop Farthing?"}},["kw"]={"agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","gallows' end tavern","lordaeron","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Coleman Farthing",["s"]="Coleman Farthing is a bitter Forsaken survivor residing in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. In life, he worked for the wealthy Agamand dynasty at their extensive flour mills in northern Tirisfal. Convinced to stay and defend the estate against the Scourge, he died alongside his fellow laborers, and now dedicates his undeath to exacting vengeance on his former masters.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, Coleman Farthing earned an honest living as a laborer at the Agamand Mills, the largest milling and agricultural operation in Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge poured across Lordaeron, the aristocratic Agamand family refused to flee their valuable lands. Instead, they urged their household and laborers to take up arms alongside them, promising they could hold the farmsteads against the undead horde. Coleman and his fellow workers stayed, believing their masters—a decision that cost every last one of them their lives.",["t"]="A Bitter Servant"},{["b"]="Raised into undeath only to break free under the banner of the Forsaken, Coleman harbors a burning hatred for the Agamands. Rather than blaming only the Scourge, he blames the sheer hubris and greed of his employers for tricking their staff into an impossible last stand. Now loitering in Brill's tavern, Coleman enlists Horde champions to march into the blighted mills, cut down the risen Agamand kin, and shatter the heirloom relics housed within their family crypt so that their legacy is utterly erased.",["t"]="Vengeance from the Grave"}}}}}
t["npc:collin-mauren"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,339,21.458.0,23.439.0,28.460.0,33.142.0,45.245.0,59.174.0,52.200.0,53.201.0,37.218.0",["h"]="dfc0b3",["n"]="Collin Mauren",["s"]="Collin Mauren. Collin Mauren es un mago humano que reside en el Barrio de los Magos, en la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Como erudito investigador y creador de encantamientos, experimenta con componentes naturales exóticos para concebir hechizos de utilidad únicos. Entre sus ocupaciones está ayudar a su conocido, el ingeniero y explorador gnomo Gaxim Silvóxido, con pergaminos arcanos especializados. Ubicado en el bullicioso Barrio de los Magos de Ventormenta, Collin Mauren pasa sus días dedicándose a las aplicaciones más tranquilas y prácticas de la magia. En lugar de perseguir el poder elemental en estado puro, se centra en elaborar fórmulas arcanas que resuelvan problemas logísticos concretos. Collin suele recurrir a anomalías naturales y componentes brutos recolectados por todo Azeroth, entrelazando sus propiedades intrínsecas en pergaminos mágicos funcionales y reactivos tanto para amigos como para viajeros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Collin exemplifies the experimental craft of spell creation, demonstrating how earthly reagents like elemental debris and basilisk scales can be harnessed to weave utility magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="Collin facilitates communication and trade across the Alliance by supplying adventurers with utility magic spanning from Westfall to Kalimdor.",["race:Human"]="Living quietly in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Collin represents the scholarly pursuits of human wizards who study the broader world from the heart of the capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Collin Mauren is located in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City, tucked among the towers and shops frequented by the capital's arcane scholars.",["al"]={"collin mauren location","where is collin mauren","collin mauren stormwind"},["q"]="Where can Collin Mauren be found?"},{["a"]="Collin specializes in applied enchantments and utility spells. Rather than combat evocations, he experiments with raw natural components—such as elemental debris and beast scales—to devise long-distance messaging scrolls and unique dweomers.",["al"]={"collin mauren research","what does collin mauren do","collin mauren magic"},["q"]="What kind of magic does Collin specialize in?"},{["a"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an adventurous gnome tinkerer and a friend of Collin. Collin supports Gaxim's distant journeys by providing him with custom-crafted communication scrolls.",["al"]={"gaxim rustfizzle friend","collin and gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle"},["q"]="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle and how is Collin connected to him?"},{["a"]="Collin uses the essence of Westfall's elemental Dust Devils to power a messaging spell. The windy debris of the elementals carries the harmonic energy required to craft reliable communication scrolls.",["al"]={"devils in westfall quest","why dust devils","westfall dust devils quest"},["q"]="Why does Collin need elemental debris from Westfall?"},{["a"]="Collin studies the magical properties of basilisk scales native to the Stonetalon Mountains in Kalimdor. He uses their sturdy, naturally resistant hides as reagent bases to synthesize new incantations.",["al"]={"stonetalon basilisks","retrieval for mauren","stonetalon scales collin"},["q"]="Why is Collin interested in the Stonetalon Mountains?"},{["a"]="While Collin resides in the Mage Quarter and practices the traditions common among Alliance wizards, he functions primarily as an independent researcher and reagent crafter rather than an active Dalaran representative.",["al"]={"is collin kirin tor","collin mauren dalaran","mage quarter collin"},["q"]="Is Collin aligned with the Kirin Tor?"}},["kw"]={"basilisk","collin mauren","dust devils","gaxim rustfizzle","mage quarter","stonetalon","stormwind","westfall"},["n"]="Collin Mauren",["s"]="Collin Mauren is a human mage residing in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City. A scholarly researcher and crafter of incantations, he experiments with exotic natural reagents to devise unique utility spells. Among his pursuits is assisting his acquaintance, the gnome engineer and explorer Gaxim Rustfizzle, with specialized arcane scrolls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within Stormwind's bustling Mage Quarter, Collin Mauren spends his days pursuing the quieter, more practical applications of magic. Rather than chasing raw elemental power, he focuses on crafting arcane formulas that solve specific, logistical problems. Collin often turns to natural anomalies and raw components scavenged across Azeroth, weaving their intrinsic properties into functional magic scrolls and reagents for friends and travelers alike.",["t"]="Scholar of the Arcane"},{["b"]="Collin maintains a close correspondence and friendship with the gnomish tinker Gaxim Rustfizzle. When Gaxim needed a reliable way to communicate across great distances during his travels, Collin designed a specialized messaging spell. To anchor the spell, he utilizes the whirling debris left behind by Westfall's erratic Dust Devils, capturing the essence of shifting wind to ensure long-distance messages reach his adventurous colleague.",["t"]="Aiding Gaxim Rustfizzle"},{["b"]="Beyond his work with local elementals, Collin's research extends clear across the Great Sea to the crags of Kalimdor. Curiously captivated by the resilient hides of basilisks native to the Stonetalon Mountains, Collin seeks out their scales to synthesize new spells. Travelers venturing into Kalimdor frequently receive his requests for these rare hides, fueling Collin's ongoing fascination with how primal creature anatomy can stabilize complex enchantments.",["t"]="Exotic Studies in Stonetalon"}}}}}
t["npc:commander-springvale"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,361,20.303.0,14.359.0,15.361.0,37.225.0,33.205.0,53.181.0,44.185.0,19.138.0,34.139.0",["h"]="67634d",["n"]="Comandante Vallefont",["s"]="Comandante Vallefont. El Comandante Vallefont fue en su momento un devoto paladín y el líder de la guardia armada del Barón Filargenta en el Castillo de Colmillo Oscuro. Asesinado junto a sus hombres durante la matanza de huargen salvajes orquestada por el archimago Arugal, su espíritu vengativo permanece allí para atormentar las estancias del castillo. Incluso tras su muerte, su fantasma custodia con fiereza la fortaleza y busca venganza para su señor caído. Antes de la ruina del Castillo de Colmillo Oscuro, el Comandante Vallefont destacaba como un honorable paladín dedicado a la Luz Sagrada y un juramentado defensor del Barón Filargenta. Al mando de la guarnición en el Bosque de Argénteos, supervisó la seguridad de la fortaleza durante los difíciles días posteriores a la caída de Lordaeron a manos de la Plaga.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Springvale is a sobering reminder of how duty and sacred vows can curdle into eternal torment when an honorable knight is bound to a corrupted grave.",["faction:Alliance"]="Springvale represents the lost soldiers of Lordaeron and Gilneas, loyal defenders who fell not to the Scourge directly, but to the reckless summonings meant to stop them.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken reclaiming Silverpine Forest, laying the commander's shade to rest is another step in purging the remnants of Arugal's tragic failure."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Commander Springvale was a paladin of the Holy Light who served as the commander of Baron Silverlaine's armed forces. He was tasked with the defense of Shadowfang Keep and remained fiercely loyal to the Baron until his death.",["al"]={"springvale backstory","who is commander springvale","is springvale a paladin"},["q"]="Who was Commander Springvale in life?"},{["a"]="He was killed when Archmage Arugal summoned feral worgen to fight the Scourge. The untamed beasts turned upon the inhabitants of Shadowfang Keep, massacring Baron Silverlaine, Springvale, and the garrison.",["al"]={"how did springvale die","who killed springvale","springvale death"},["q"]="How did Commander Springvale die?"},{["a"]="Twisted in death, his spirit remains bound by his final oaths. Springvale's ghost wanders the halls to defend the ruins and seek vengeance for his fallen lord against all who enter.",["al"]={"why is springvale a ghost","springvale motive","why does springvale fight"},["q"]="Why is Commander Springvale haunting Shadowfang Keep?"},{["a"]="The violent trauma of his death and the dark magic pervading the keep corrupted his spirit. In his spectral state, the holy vows he once wielded have warped into vengeful, unholy power.",["al"]={"why unholy magic","springvale unholy abilities","corrupted paladin"},["q"]="Why does a former paladin use unholy powers?"},{["a"]="Commander Springvale served Baron Silverlaine, the noble ruler and master of Shadowfang Keep before Arugal's beasts devastated the estate.",["al"]={"springvale master","who did springvale serve","springvale and silverlaine"},["q"]="Who was his master?"},{["a"]="Commander Springvale's ghost is encountered deep within the keep, haunting the fortified chambers near the castle chapel and council rooms.",["al"]={"springvale location","where is springvale","shadowfang springvale room"},["q"]="Where in the keep can he be found?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","commander","ghost","paladin","shadowfang","silverlaine","silverpine","springvale","worgen"},["n"]="Commander Springvale",["s"]="Commander Springvale was once a devoted paladin and the head of Baron Silverlaine's armed guard at Shadowfang Keep. Slain alongside his men during the feral worgen slaughter orchestrated by Archmage Arugal, his vengeful spirit remains behind to haunt the castle halls. Even in death, his ghost fiercely guards the keep and seeks vengeance for his fallen master.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the ruin of Shadowfang Keep, Commander Springvale stood as an honorable paladin dedicated to the Holy Light and a sworn defender of Baron Silverlaine. Leading the garrison in Silverpine Forest, he oversaw the keep's security during the fraught days following the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge.",["t"]="The Fallen Commander"},{["b"]="When Archmage Arugal summoned the extraplanar worgen to repel the undead Scourge encroaching upon Gilnean soil, the wild beasts quickly slipped from the mage's control. The ravenous pack descended upon the fortress, slaughtering Baron Silverlaine and his entire guard. Springvale perished in the halls he had sworn to protect, his service violently cut short.",["t"]="Arugal's Folly"},{["b"]="Death offered no release to Springvale's bound soul. Twisted by trauma and necromantic energy, his ghost lingers within the keep's stone chambers. Though he carried the teachings of the Light in life, his phantom now strikes out with unholy power, blindly executing an eternal duty to avenge the slain Baron against any trespasser who sets foot inside the keep.",["t"]="An Unholy Vigil"}}}}}
t["npc:cookie"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,336,22.465.0,13.468.0,49.256.0,43.207.0,43.203.0,46.195.0,40.147.0,44.150.0",["h"]="0c079e",["n"]="El Chef",["s"]="El Chef. El Chef es un múrloc de élite que ejerce de cocinero del barco a bordo del acorazado oculto en lo profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte. Un recluta inusual dentro de la Hermandad Defias, cuida los calderos de la tripulación bajo la atenta mirada del Capitán Verdetez y de Edwin VanCleef. Es el único jefe completamente opcional que se encuentra en el dique seco subterráneo. Bajo las cubiertas del imponente acorazado en la Cala del Acorazado, las tareas culinarias no recaen en un batidor humano ni en un ingeniero goblin, sino en un múrloc solitario conocido simplemente como El Chef. La forma en que consiguió el puesto sigue siendo un secreto que solo guarda el mismísimo Edwin VanCleef. Sean cuales sean las dudas que el resto de la tripulación pueda albergar acerca de que un múrloc gestione sus raciones, los piratas rara vez están en posición de ser quisquillosos, y en los bajos fondos de Arroyo de la Luna, comida es comida.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef's rogue network relies on strange, unconventional assets, and Cookie proves that even the Brotherhood's supply lines feature odd surprises.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's scouts are often surprised to find murlocs actively working within the Defias leadership rather than merely infesting Westfall's outer shores.",["profession:Cooking"]="Finding a murloc appointed as chief cook aboard an outlaw juggernaut is a testament to the desperate, unrefined standards of pirate cuisine."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Edwin VanCleef is the only one who knows why Cookie was recruited and granted the galley duties. The Defias outlaws and goblin shipwrights simply accept the arrangement because pirate crews take food where they can get it, regardless of the chef's species.",["al"]={"why murloc cook","why is cookie on the ship","cookie defias lore"},["q"]="Why is a murloc working as a cook for the Defias?"},{["a"]="Cookie is located in the Ironclad Cove at the very end of the Deadmines. He patrols the shallow water and docks near the stern of the giant wooden juggernaut, just past the ramp where Mr. Smite stands guard.",["al"]={"where is cookie","cookie location deadmines","finding cookie"},["q"]="Where can Cookie be found in the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="No, Cookie is the only optional boss in the dungeon. Infiltrators can board the vessel directly to confront Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef without ever disturbing the cook's patrol along the shore.",["al"]={"is cookie optional","do you have to kill cookie","cookie skip"},["q"]="Is Cookie required to finish the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="Cookie is not associated with any of the known local murloc tribes, such as those along the Westfall coast. He lives and works entirely among the outlaws and scoundrels of the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"what tribe is cookie","cookie murloc tribe"},["q"]="Does Cookie belong to a specific murloc tribe?"},{["a"]="Cookie wields cooking implements in melee combat and can hurl caustic splashes of acid at attackers, burning them with dangerous culinary mixtures.",["al"]={"cookie abilities","how does cookie fight","cookie attacks"},["q"]="What weapons or attacks does Cookie use?"},{["a"]="Cookie directly serves the naval arm of the Defias Brotherhood under the command of Captain Greenskin, answering ultimately to Edwin VanCleef himself.",["al"]={"cookie boss","who leads cookie","cookie greenskin vancleef"},["q"]="Who does Cookie report to on the juggernaut?"}},["kw"]={"captain greenskin","cook","cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaut","murloc"},["n"]="Cookie",["s"]="Cookie is an elite murloc serving as the ship's cook aboard the juggernaut hidden deep within the Deadmines. An unusual recruit among the Defias Brotherhood, he tends the crew's cauldrons beneath the watchful eye of Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef. He is the only entirely optional boss encountered within the underground dry dock.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Beneath the decks of the towering juggernaut in the Ironclad Cove, cooking duty falls neither to a human outrider nor a goblin engineer, but to a solitary murloc known simply as Cookie. How he secured the position remains a private secret kept by Edwin VanCleef himself. Whatever doubts the rest of the crew might harbor about a murloc presiding over their rations, pirates are rarely in a position to be picky, and in the underworld of Moonbrook, a meal is a meal.",["t"]="The Brotherhood's Chef"},{["b"]="Cookie patrols the waterways and shores around the pirate flagship, wielding his cooking utensils alongside acidic brews. Despite being isolated from typical murloc tribes, he defends his cauldron with savage ferocity, flinging caustic concoctions at any intruders who wander into the docks. Because his station sits away from the main gangplanks, many who storm the cove bypass his kitchen entirely, making him the only optional overseer aboard the Defias juggernaut.",["t"]="A Bitter Brew"}}}}}
t["npc:corithras-moonrage"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,376,19.376.0,18.389.0,26.394.1,26.211.0,38.125.0,47.222.0,54.273.0,42.167.0,59.168.0",["h"]="caa2d2",["n"]="Coriithas Furia Lunar",["s"]="Coriithas Furia Lunar. Coriithas Furia Lunar es un erudito elfo de la noche y asignador de misiones apostado en la aldea de Dolanaar, en Teldrassil. Guía a los aventureros recién llegados para que comprendan la naturaleza del gran Árbol del Mundo y les encomienda la tarea de mantener sus pozos de la luna sagrados. A través de sus enseñanzas, revela tanto la importancia espiritual de Teldrassil como las crecientes cargas que soportan los kaldorei. Afincado en el sombrío asentamiento de Dolanaar, Coriithas Furia Lunar ejerce de instructor para los viajeros que abandonan los confines protegidos de Cañada Umbría. A medida que los jóvenes kaldorei se adentran en las ramas más extensas de Teldrassil, Coriithas se asegura de que comprendan la historia de su nuevo hogar. Enseña que sobrevivir en esta era cambiante requiere vigilancia y reverencia hacia el orden natural.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Corithras's tasks deeply connected to their calling, as his moonwell rites directly track the health and creeping ailments of the World Tree.",["class:Priest"]="Priests of Elune assist Corithras in carrying the blessed waters of the moonwells, maintaining the spiritual and physical harmony of Dolanaar's surrounding wilds.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, speaking with Corithras is a foundational lesson in the post-Third War reality, confronting the loss of ancient immortality and the disputed creation of Teldrassil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar located in Dolanaar. He introduces adventurers to the history of Teldrassil and tasks them with tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the waters of the World Tree.",["al"]={"corithras moonrage role","who is corithras","dolanaar quest giver"},["q"]="Who is Corithras Moonrage?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing outdoors in Dolanaar, the central crossroads village situated in the southern reaches of Teldrassil.",["al"]={"corithras location","where is corithras","find corithras"},["q"]="Where can Corithras Moonrage be found?"},{["a"]="The Crown of the Earth quests involve drawing water from moonwells across Teldrassil. Corithras combines the collected water for delivery to Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, where the druids need to replenish their moonwell.",["al"]={"crown of the earth meaning","corithras quests","moonwell quests"},["q"]="What is the Crown of the Earth questline about?"},{["a"]="Corithras shares the history of how Teldrassil was planted after the Third War to restore night elven immortality. Because the Dragon Aspects refused to bless the tree, Corithras remains acutely aware that the tree lacks divine protection and that his people remain mortal.",["al"]={"why burden of kaldorei","aspects refusal","why no immortality"},["q"]="Why is Corithras concerned about Teldrassil's origins?"},{["a"]="He imparts lessons on the recent sacrifices of the Third War, the founding of Teldrassil, and the responsibility each kaldorei bears to defend their new woodland home.",["al"]={"corithras lore","dolanaar history","what does corithras tell you"},["q"]="What does Corithras teach new adventurers?"},{["a"]="He serves as a loyal citizen and scholar of Darnassus in Dolanaar, working closely with druids and priests alike to monitor the well-being of the forest and its waters.",["al"]={"corithras faction","is corithras a druid"},["q"]="Is Corithras aligned with the Cenarion Circle or Darnassus?"}},["kw"]={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","kaldorei","moonwell","night elf","teldrassil"},["n"]="Corithras Moonrage",["s"]="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He guides newly arrived adventurers in understanding the nature of the great World Tree and tasks them with maintaining its sacred moonwells. Through his lessons, he reveals both the spiritual importance of Teldrassil and the growing burdens carried by the kaldorei.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Residing in the shaded settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage serves as an instructor to travelers leaving the sheltered bounds of Shadowglen. As young kaldorei venture into the wider boughs of Teldrassil, Corithras ensures they understand the history of their new home. He teaches that survival in this changing era requires vigilance and reverence for the natural order.",["t"]="Scholar of Dolanaar"},{["b"]="Much of Corithras's duty revolves around collecting moonwell water for the druids in Darnassus. He directs adventurers to collect pure waters from moonwells across Teldrassil in specially crafted phials for delivery to Fandral Staghelm. Through these trials, he monitors the health of the World Tree and seeks to maintain the delicate balance of the wilderness against creeping corruption.",["t"]="Crown of the Earth"},{["b"]="Beneath Corithras's guidance lies an uneasy truth regarding Teldrassil's creation. Unlike the ancient Nordrassil, this new World Tree was raised without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, who refused Fandral Staghelm's ambitious creation. Corithras reflects on the loss of night elven immortality and the fragile, uncertain future the kaldorei now face under the boughs of an unblessed bough.",["t"]="The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}}}}
t["npc:dalar-dawnweaver"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,419,17.525.0,32.503.0,24.268.0,42.265.0,40.245.0,46.275.0,45.248.0,36.186.0",["h"]="7e4143",["n"]="Dalar Tejalba",["s"]="Dalar Tejalba. Dalar Tejalba es un antiguo archimago de Dalaran que ahora sirve a los Renegados en El Sepulcro, en el Bosque de Argénteos. Asesinado durante la destrucción de la ciudad de los magos a manos de la Plaga y liberado más tarde del control del Rey Exánime, enfoca su intelecto mágico en analizar las amenazas regionales. Desde las sombras de la tumba, dirige los esfuerzos para comprender la persistente presencia de Dalaran y poner fin a la locura del archimago Arugal. En vida, Dalar Tejalba ostentaba un alto rango en el Kirin Tor y recorría las estancias de la Ciudadela Violeta cuando Dalaran era la cumbre del dominio arcano. Su vida mortal llegó a su fin cuando la Plaga saqueó la ciudad para preparar la invocación de Archimonde. Reanimado como un siervo descerebrado del Rey Exánime, Dalar se liberó junto a Lady Sylvanas Brisaveloz cuando el dominio de la Plaga decayó. Ahora apostado en El Sepulcro, conserva el agudo intelecto de un archimago, volcado por completo en proteger el reino de los Renegados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages will find in Dalar a dark mirror of Dalaran's former grandeur, demonstrating how Kirin Tor training can be weaponized in service to the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed at the Sepulcher, Dalar secures the Horde's western frontier by coordinating strikes against the worgen of Shadowfang Keep and hostile Kirin Tor enclaves.",["race:Undead"]="Dalar exemplifies the reclaimed agency of the Forsaken, turning the very knowledge he possessed in life against Dalaran remnants and rogue wizards who threaten their sovereignty."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage found at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. In life, he was an archmage of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. After dying during the Third War and being raised by the Scourge, he broke free of the Lich King's control to serve the Dark Lady.",["al"]={"who is dalar","dalar dawnweaver lore","dalar background"},["q"]="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?"},{["a"]="Dalar was present in Dalaran when Arthas Menethil and the Scourge invaded to recover the Book of Medivh. Slain during the assault as Kel'Thuzad summoned Archimonde into Azeroth, Dalar was raised into undeath as a servant of the Scourge until Sylvanas liberated him.",["al"]={"how did dalar die","dalar death","dalar third war"},["q"]="What happened to him during the Third War?"},{["a"]="He serves as the local arcane authority for the Forsaken in Silverpine Forest. His historical familiarity with both the Kirin Tor forces occupying Ambermill and his former peer, Archmage Arugal, makes him ideally suited to counter those threats.",["al"]={"why is dalar in sepulcher","dalar role in silverpine"},["q"]="Why is Dalar stationed at the Sepulcher?"},{["a"]="Both were mages of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran before its fall. Dalar recognizes the tragic descent and lethal danger of Arugal's summoning experiments in Shadowfang Keep, tasking adventurers with gathering relics of Arugal's folly and ultimately demanding the mad mage's death.",["al"]={"dalar and arugal","did dalar know arugal"},["q"]="What is Dalar's connection to Archmage Arugal?"},{["a"]="Dalar keeps a watchful eye on his former homeland and the surviving Kirin Tor forces stationed at Ambermill. He directs agents to intercept their communications and analyze their intentions to ensure they cannot threaten the Forsaken in Silverpine.",["al"]={"dalar and dalaran","dalar ambermill"},["q"]="What does Dalar want with Dalaran's remnants?"},{["a"]="No. While he was once an archmage among them, his loyalty now lies with the Forsaken and the Horde. He actively opposes the surviving Kirin Tor forces operating within Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"is dalar kirin tor","is dalar loyal to dalaran"},["q"]="Is Dalar aligned with the Kirin Tor?"}},["kw"]={"archmage","arugal","dalar","dalaran","dawnweaver","forsaken","kirin tor","sepulcher","silverpine"},["n"]="Dalar Dawnweaver",["s"]="Dalar Dawnweaver is a former archmage of Dalaran who now serves the Forsaken at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Slain during the Scourge's destruction of the magi's city and later freed from the Lich King's control, he turns his magical intellect toward dissecting regional threats. From the shadows of the tomb, he directs efforts to understand Dalaran's lingering presence and undo the madness of Archmage Arugal.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In life, Dalar Dawnweaver held high rank among the Kirin Tor, walking the halls of the Violet Citadel when Dalaran was a pinnacle of arcane mastery. His mortal life ended when the Scourge sacked the city to pave the way for Archimonde's summoning. Reanimated into the mindless thrall of the Lich King, Dalar broke free alongside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner when the Scourge's grip faltered. Now stationed at the Sepulcher, he retains the piercing intellect of an archmage, turned entirely toward safeguarding the Forsaken realm.",["t"]="A Fallen Archmage"},{["b"]="Silverpine Forest is caught between multiple perils, and Dalar serves as the Sepulcher's arcane strategist. To the south, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill under a protective dome, meddling in matters Dalar seeks to uncover and disrupt. Even closer looms Shadowfang Keep and the feral worgen loosed upon the woods. Dalar possesses intimate knowledge of his former colleague, Archmage Arugal, and meticulously orchestrates campaigns to neutralize Arugal's beastly creations before they overrun the region.",["t"]="Eyes on Ambermill and Shadowfang"}}}}}
t["npc:daphne-stilwell"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,287,20.475.0,21.485.0,18.451.1,23.211.0,27.183.0,51.248.0,40.226.0,26.163.0,31.157.0",["h"]="640164",["n"]="Daphne Fontana",["s"]="Daphne Fontana. Daphne Fontana cuida de un huerto aislado en lo alto de los acantilados costeros de Páramos de Poniente con vistas a Playa Larga. Junto a su esposo Jordan, huyó del caos del norte y se trasladó al sur, colaborando discretamente con la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada mientras defiende su hogar de los forajidos de los alrededores. Encaramada a los riscos al oeste de Arroyo de la Luna y la salida de Las Minas de la Muerte, Daphne Fontana regenta una granja y un huerto de manzanos retirados. Desde abajo, a lo largo de Playa Larga, o desde arriba en las rutas de grifos hacia el sur rumbo a la Vega de Tuercespina, la pequeña granja parece tranquila y modesta. Sin embargo, llevar una hacienda en los Páramos de Poniente actuales dista mucho de ser seguro. A pesar del asedio de los bandidos y los carroñeros errantes, Daphne trabaja con esmero sus árboles y vigila su aislado pedazo de tierra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Daphne Stilwell is a vital figure in the trials of the Tome of Valor; defending her from ruthless Defias marauders proves a paladin's devotion to protecting the innocent.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Stilwells embody the plight of displaced northern refugees who continue to serve the Alliance and the Church of the Holy Light despite the perils of the Westfall frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Daphne Stilwell is a human homesteader living in an isolated farmhouse above Westfall's Longshore. She is the wife of the famed blacksmith Jordan Stilwell, with whom she escaped the devastated northern kingdoms.",["al"]={"who is daphne","daphne stilwell info","stilwell wife"},["q"]="Who is Daphne Stilwell?"},{["a"]="Daphne previously lived in the north near Pyrewood Village and worked at what is now known as Shadowfang Keep before calamity drove her and Jordan southward to the lands of Stormwind.",["al"]={"daphne origin","where is daphne from","is daphne gilnean"},["q"]="Where did Daphne come from?"},{["a"]="Her farm sits on the cliffs directly overlooking the southern waters of Westfall, right above the exit tunnels of the Deadmines. Its proximity to the Defias stronghold makes it an easy target for outlaws looking to raid supplies or remove meddlers.",["al"]={"why do defias attack daphne","defias farm attack","stilwell farm bandits"},["q"]="Why is her farm attacked by the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Her husband Jordan aids the Church of the Holy Light by forging sanctified weapons. As part of their trials for the Tome of Valor, paladins of the Silver Hand are dispatched to Westfall to safeguard Daphne from bandit attacks.",["al"]={"paladin quest daphne","tome of valor daphne","why do paladins visit daphne"},["q"]="What is Daphne's connection to paladins?"},{["a"]="Yes. When the Defias assault her orchard, she does not cower; she draws a weapon and directly battles the attackers alongside any paladins defending the homestead.",["al"]={"does daphne fight","is daphne a warrior"},["q"]="Can Daphne defend herself?"},{["a"]="Her farm is tucked on the clifftops of south-western Westfall, situated southwest of Moonbrook near the Deadmines secret cove exit overlooking the Longshore.",["al"]={"where is daphne farm","how to get to stilwell farm","daphne stilwell location"},["q"]="How do you reach her farmhouse?"}},["kw"]={"daphne stilwell","defias brotherhood","jordan stilwell","longshore","orchard","pyrewood village","shadowfang keep","tome of valor","westfall"},["n"]="Daphne Stilwell",["s"]="Daphne Stilwell tends an isolated orchard nestled atop the coastal cliffs of Westfall overlooking the Longshore. Together with her husband Jordan, she fled turmoil in the north and relocated south, quietly aiding the Church of the Holy Light while defending her home from nearby outlaws.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the bluffs to the west of Moonbrook and the exit of the Deadmines, Daphne Stilwell manages a secluded homestead and apple orchard. From below along the Longshore or above on gryphon routes south to Stranglethorn Vale, the small farm looks quiet and unassuming. Yet running a homestead in modern Westfall is anything but safe. Despite the encroaching bandits and roaming scavengers, Daphne diligently works her trees and keeps watch over her isolated patch of land.",["t"]="A Life on the Cliffs"},{["b"]="Before settling in the hills of Westfall, Daphne and her husband Jordan lived in Lordaeron near Pyrewood Village, working in what is now Shadowfang Keep. When darkness and disaster overtook the region, they were driven southward along with thousands of other human refugees. In Stormwind's orbit, Jordan's renowned craftsmanship and Daphne's steady presence led them to forge close ties with the Church of the Holy Light, providing support and holy arms to paladins of the Silver Hand.",["t"]="Refugees of the North"},{["b"]="Living so close to the Deadmines puts Daphne square in the path of the Defias Brotherhood. While Jordan travels or labors on forging holy weaponry outside the capital, Daphne is frequently left to maintain their coastal home alone. When brigands raided the farmstead seeking retribution or plunder, Daphne picked up arms and fought alongside aspiring paladins sent by the Cathedral, proving herself remarkably fierce and capable in the heat of battle.",["t"]="Defending the Farm"}}}}}
t["npc:dark-iron-ambassador"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,252,15.383.0,24.453.1,32.221.0,43.256.0,53.265.0,36.194.0,36.212.0,44.135.0",["h"]="b8ad1d",["n"]="Embajador Hierro Negro",["s"]="Embajador Hierro Negro. En lo profundo de las salas irradiadas de Gnomeregan acecha el Embajador Hierro Negro, un esquivo emisario enviado por el emperador Dagran Thaurissan. Su presencia revela que la caída de la capital gnoma entraña mucho más que simples incursiones salvajes de troggs y locura. Aunque públicamente se culpa de la catastrófica caída de Gnomeregan a la invasión de los troggs y a la desesperada estratagema de radiación del Manitas Mayor Mekkatorque, la presencia del Embajador Hierro Negro apunta a maquinaciones mucho más oscuras. Al vagar por las profundidades contaminadas de los pasillos de los talleres, este enano Hierro Negro poco común sugiere que Sicco Termochufe no traicionó a su pueblo en completo aislamiento.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The ambassador's secret dealings with Thermaplugg represent an active hostile front right on the doorstep of Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your ancient Dark Iron kin have wormed their way into the gnome halls, demonstrating that Thaurissan's reach threatens Khaz Modan from within.",["race:Gnome"]="Finding a Dark Iron envoy in Gnomeregan proves the horrific betrayal that poisoned your home was backed by dwarf enemies from Blackrock."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is an envoy of the Dark Iron clan found deep inside the irradiated ruin of Gnomeregan. His role is that of a diplomatic representative between Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and the rogue forces controlling the fallen city.",["al"]={"who is this dwarf","dark iron ambassador identity","what is dark iron ambassador"},["q"]="Who is the Dark Iron Ambassador?"},{["a"]="His presence strongly suggests secret negotiations between the Dark Iron clan and the mad usurper Sicco Thermaplugg. The Dark Irons appear to have had a hand in assisting Thermaplugg or exploiting Gnomeregan's disaster for their own ends against Ironforge.",["al"]={"why are dark irons in gnomeregan","what is he doing here","dark iron dwarf purpose"},["q"]="Why is a Dark Iron dwarf inside Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="While the trogg invasion itself drove the initial crisis, in-universe conspiracies and goblin observers suggest the Dark Irons secretly assisted Thermaplugg. They may have aided in drilling operations or provided technical help with advanced subterranean equipment.",["al"]={"did dark irons cause trogg invasion","dark iron conspiracy","did thaurissan help thermaplugg"},["q"]="Did the Dark Irons help cause the fall of Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="He represents the Dark Iron clan, ruled by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan from their stronghold beneath the Blackrock Mountain. He was dispatched to treat with Gnomeregan's traitorous new leadership.",["al"]={"where is ambassador from","who sent him","who does he work for"},["q"]="Where does the ambassador come from?"},{["a"]="Yes, evidence strongly points to an alliance. As an envoy, his survival among Thermaplugg's leper gnomes and mechanostriders demonstrates an ongoing diplomatic link rather than hostility between the two factions.",["al"]={"thermaplugg dark iron ally","is he with thermaplugg","working with thermaplugg"},["q"]="Is he allied with Sicco Thermaplugg?"},{["a"]="He is an elusive, rare encounter who wanders the contaminated engineering sectors and workshop corridors inside the Gnomeregan dungeon.",["al"]={"ambassador spawn location","where does he spawn","ambassador gnomeregan location"},["q"]="Where can the Dark Iron Ambassador be found?"}},["kw"]={"conspiracy","dark iron ambassador","dark iron clan","gnomeregan","super rig","thaurissan","thermaplugg"},["n"]="Dark Iron Ambassador",["s"]="Deep within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan lurks the Dark Iron Ambassador, an elusive emissary sent by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan. His presence reveals that the fall of the gnome capital involves far more than just wild trogg incursions and madness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Gnomeregan's catastrophic downfall is publicly blamed on the trogg invasion and High Tinker Mekkatorque's desperate radiation gambit, the presence of the Dark Iron Ambassador points to far darker machinations. Wandering the contaminated depths of the workshop corridors, this rare Dark Iron dwarf suggests that Sicco Thermaplugg did not betray his people in complete isolation.",["t"]="A Shadowy Envoy"},{["b"]="The true motives behind Emperor Thaurissan's envoy remain cloaked in secrecy and speculation. Both Alliance investigators in Ironforge and Horde-affiliated goblins have raised theories about the Dark Iron clan's involvement in the subterranean disaster. Rumors swirl that the Dark Irons offered technical expertise, aided Thermaplugg in operating heavy machinery like the subterranean super rig, or brokered a vile pact to undercut Ironforge from below.",["t"]="Conspiracies in the Deep"}}}}}
t["npc:darsok-swiftdagger"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,370,27.449.0,24.425.1,24.426.0,36.164.0,30.202.0,27.182.0,52.205.0,48.147.0,36.165.0",["h"]="3128f3",["n"]="Darsok Movedaga",["s"]="Darsok Movedaga. Darsok Movedaga es un guerrero y explorador orco apostado en El Cruce, en pleno corazón de Los Baldíos. Conocido por su feroz odio hacia las arpías, dirige a los aventureros de la Horda hacia el norte, a Las Colinas Áridas, para desarticular el matriarcado aviar que hostiga a viajeros y asentamientos. Mantiene contactos por todas las llanuras y actúa como un intermediario de confianza para el médico brujo Jin'Zil en Malaka'jin. En medio del bullicioso enclave de El Cruce, Darsok Movedaga vigila atentamente las amenazas que surgen del matorral septentrional. La arteria comercial que conecta Durotar, Mulgore y las regiones del norte se encuentra bajo un asedio constante, no solo por parte de saqueadores y centauros, sino también de cazadoras aéreas organizadas. Darsok concentra su ira en las arpías Alabruja, cuyos nidos en Las Colinas Áridas, al noroeste de Las Charcas del Olvido, amenazan directamente a las caravanas del norte.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Living up to the name Swiftdagger, Darsok favors precise, lethal decapitation strikes against enemy leadership rather than grinding attrition.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers, Darsok provides crucial early tactical missions that secure the crossroads trade routes against aerial ambush.",["race:Orc"]="Darsok exemplifies the focused, martial mindset of orcs tasked with taming and securing Kalimdor's perilous frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Darsok Swiftdagger is stationed in the Crossroads, the central Horde settlement in the Barrens. He stands ready to direct passing travelers toward northern threats.",["al"]={"darsok location","where is darsok swiftdagger","find darsok","darsok swiftdagger spot"},["q"]="Where is Darsok Swiftdagger located?"},{["a"]="The Witchwing harpies roost in the canyons northwest of the Forgotten Pools and pose a constant predatory danger to Horde caravans, travelers, and scouts moving along the northern trails of the Barrens.",["al"]={"why kill harpies","darsok harpy grudge","witchwing harpies barrens"},["q"]="Why is Darsok hunting harpies?"},{["a"]="Serena Bloodfeather is the cruel matriarch leading the Witchwing harpies of the Dry Hills. Darsok tasks adventurers with slaying her to shatter the cohesion and command of the flock.",["al"]={"serena bloodfeather","harpy leader barrens","witchwing leader"},["q"]="Who is Serena Bloodfeather?"},{["a"]="Darsok is an ally and correspondent of Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, a Darkspear troll stationed at Malaka'jin. He facilitates communications and sends adventurers carrying missives to Jin'Zil's remote encampment.",["al"]={"jin'zil letter","darsok and jin'zil","witch doctor jin'zil connection"},["q"]="What is Darsok's connection to Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?"},{["a"]="Darsok organizes his harpy campaign from the Crossroads. No Classic source here identifies either Sergra Darkthorn or Thork as his direct superior.",["al"]={"darsok thork","who does darsok answer to","crossroads leadership"},["q"]="Does Darsok report to Sergra Darkthorn or Thork?"},{["a"]="The Witchwing harpies roost in the Dry Hills, a series of jagged ravines and cliffs situated northwest of the Forgotten Pools in the northern reaches of the Barrens.",["al"]={"witchwing location","dry hills harpies","where to find harpies barrens"},["q"]="Where do the Witchwing harpies nest?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","bloodfeather","crossroads","darsok","harpy","jin'zil","serena","swiftdagger","thork","witchwing"},["n"]="Darsok Swiftdagger",["s"]="Darsok Swiftdagger is an orc warrior and scout stationed at the Crossroads in the heart of the Barrens. Known for his fierce hatred of harpies, he directs Horde adventurers north into the Dry Hills to break the avian matriarchy harassing travelers and settlements. He maintains ties across the plains, serving as a trusted contact for Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Malaka'jin.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Amid the bustling hub of the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger keeps a sharp eye on the threats creeping out of the northern scrubland. The trade artery connecting Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern reaches is under constant siege, not only from raiders and centaur, but from organized aerial hunters. Darsok focuses his wrath on the Witchwing harpies, whose roosts in the Dry Hills northwest of the Forgotten Pools directly threaten northern caravans.",["t"]="A Watcher at the Crossroads"},{["b"]="Darsok does not merely defend the roads; he coordinates targeted strikes deep into harpy territory. His campaign begins by thinning the aggressive Harpy Raiders before tasking hardened fighters with executing lieutenants and ultimately taking the head of their matriarch, Serena Bloodfeather. By systematically dismantling their leadership, Swiftdagger aims to leave the predatory flock broken and scattered across the crags.",["t"]="The War on the Witchwing"},{["b"]="While his immediate duties center around harpy eradication, Darsok Swiftdagger serves as an important point of contact within the Horde network. He maintains correspondence with Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, the enigmatic troll residing at Malaka'jin on the border of the Stonetalon Mountains. Messages and intelligence carried through Darsok help ensure that outlying enclaves stay informed of developments across the central plains.",["t"]="Connections in the Scrub"}}}}}
t["npc:deathguard-dillinger"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,251,17.361.0,24.352.0,27.354.1,38.121.0,35.205.0,43.199.0,44.153.0,54.220.0,24.189.0",["h"]="de7793",["n"]="Guardia de la Muerte Dillinger",["s"]="Guardia de la Muerte Dillinger. El Guardia de la Muerte Dillinger es un centinela Renegado apostado en Rémol, en los Claros de Tirisfal. Vigilando el perímetro de la villa, orienta a los no-muertos recién llegados hacia los servicios necesarios y encomienda a los reclutas la tarea de mantener a raya a los restos locales de la Plaga. Como miembro de la Guardia de la Muerte de los Renegados, Dillinger hace guardia a la entrada de Rémol, sirviendo tanto de protector de primera línea como de guía de orientación para los viajeros que salen de Camposanto. Proporciona indicaciones hacia los servicios del pueblo, como la posada, el ayuntamiento y los instructores locales, ayudando a los no-muertos recién despertados a orientarse en su nueva realidad bajo el mandato de la Dama Oscura.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Aspiring Forsaken warriors frequently work directly with Dillinger to test their martial mettle against the ferocious ghouls and skeletal horrors prowling the outskirts of Brill.",["faction:Horde"]="Dillinger represents the Forsaken's struggle to carve out a secure foothold in northern Lordaeron, showing Horde allies the relentless menace posed by mindless Scourge at their doorsteps.",["race:Undead"]="For newly freed Forsaken arriving from Deathknell, Dillinger is often the first face of military authority they meet, directing them toward training and their first duties in service of Sylvanas."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Deathguard Dillinger is posted on the outskirts of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades, watching the path leading into town.",["al"]={"dillinger location","where is dillinger","deathguard dillinger coordinates"},["q"]="Where can I find Deathguard Dillinger?"},{["a"]="The Deathguard serves as the military standing army and constabulary of the Forsaken, guarding settlements like Brill and the Undercity against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other regional threats.",["al"]={"what is deathguard","who are the deathguards","deathguard purpose"},["q"]="What is the role of the Deathguard?"},{["a"]="Dillinger tasks adventurers with slaying mindless Scourge wandering the surrounding fields and mills, reclaiming vital local infrastructure, and dealing with dangerous entities like Ulag the Cleaver.",["al"]={"dillinger quests","what quests does dillinger have"},["q"]="What tasks does Deathguard Dillinger offer?"},{["a"]="Yes, speaking with Dillinger allows players to request directions to essential services, profession trainers, and class mentors located throughout Brill.",["al"]={"dillinger directions","ask dillinger for help"},["q"]="Can Deathguard Dillinger provide directions?"},{["a"]="The mindless undead wandering Tirisfal remain under the thrall of the Scourge and the Lich King. Having broken free of that mental control, the Forsaken must eliminate these feral remnants to protect their own territory.",["al"]={"why fight scourge","undead fighting undead","brill ghouls"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken fighting other undead near Brill?"},{["a"]="Ulag the Cleaver is a dangerous Scourge horror tied to nearby tombs outside Brill. Dillinger coordinates with Forsaken recruits to summon and destroy Ulag to keep the surrounding area safe.",["al"]={"ulag quest","who is ulag","ulag the cleaver"},["q"]="Who is Ulag the Cleaver?"}},["kw"]={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard","deathguard dillinger","dillinger","the mills overrun","tirisfal glades","ulag the cleaver"},["n"]="Deathguard Dillinger",["s"]="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades. Standing watch over the town's perimeter, he directs newly arrived undead toward necessary services and tasks recruits with keeping the local Scourge remnants at bay.",["sec"]={{["b"]="As a member of the Forsaken Deathguard, Dillinger stands at the entrance of Brill, serving as both a frontline protector and an orienting guide for travelers emerging from Deathknell. He provides directions to town amenities such as the inn, the town hall, and local trainers, helping newly awakened undead navigate their new reality under the Dark Lady's rule.",["t"]="Sentinel of Brill"},{["b"]="Dillinger actively enlists capable adventurers to purge lingering mindless Scourge from the nearby farms and mills. Through assignments like cullling rotting ghouls and reclaiming infested facilities, he seeks to establish a buffer zone of security around Brill, ensuring the fledgling Forsaken settlements can endure against unending undead predation.",["t"]="Securing the Borderlands"},{["b"]="Beyond routine patrols, Dillinger coordinates responses against persistent Scourge threats lurking in the ruins around Brill. When summoned horrors such as Ulag the Cleaver emerge from nearby tombs or neglected homesteads, Dillinger ensures able fighters are dispatched to put the rampaging monstrosities down before they breach the settlement's borders.",["t"]="Containing Mindless Horrors"}}}}}
t["npc:delgren-the-purifier"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,326,35.474.0,23.449.1,18.429.0,28.276.0,25.142.0,52.228.0,55.246.0,29.170.0,45.194.0",["h"]="6a54f2",["n"]="Delgren el Purificador",["s"]="Delgren el Purificador. Delgren el Purificador es un paladín humano apostado en la Atalaya de Maestra, en el extremo norte de Vallefresno. Junto a sus camaradas Balthule Golpesombra y Feero Ferramán, ayuda a los elfos de la noche a purgar la magia demoníaca y la Magia de las Sombras que amenazan la frontera, centrándose en particular en el siniestro Culto de la Facción Oscura. Los paladines humanos son una visión poco común en las profundidades de los antiguos bosques de Kalimdor, pero Delgren el Purificador llegó con una misión. Vinculado al Alba Argenta, Delgren viajó hacia el oeste con un destacamento de guerreros sagrados decididos a prestar ayuda a los nuevos aliados elfos de la noche de la Alianza frente a los males residuales de demonios y vestigios de no-muertos de la Tercera Guerra. Apostado cerca de la frontera entre Costa Oscura y Vallefresno, mantiene una constante vigilancia sobre los viajeros que avanzan hacia el sur desde Auberdine.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren represents the far reach of the Holy Light on Kalimdor, demonstrating how paladins adapt their crusade against demons and dark magic far beyond the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers heading south from Darkshore, Delgren and his companions provide a reassuring military foothold along the dangerous Ashenvale road.",["race:NightElf"]="Though traditional kaldorei are often skeptical of foreign creeds, Delgren's company has earned trust through their practical crusade against the demonic cults troubling ancient ruins."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Delgren is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post along the road in northern Ashenvale. As an agent of the Argent Dawn, he assists the night elves in defending their lands from demonic corruption, cultists, and lingering shadows left in the wake of the Legion's invasion.",["al"]={"who is delgren","delgren lore","who is the paladin at maestras post"},["q"]="Who is Delgren the Purifier?"},{["a"]="Delgren stands at Maestra's Post, a small night elven outpost in northwestern Ashenvale just south of the border trail leading into Darkshore.",["al"]={"where is delgren","delgren location","delgren coordinates"},["q"]="Where can I find Delgren?"},{["a"]="Delgren journeyed west with a company of Argent Dawn paladins to offer aid to the Alliance's night elven allies. Their purpose is to help purge demonic incursions, undead remnants, and dark cults that threaten northern Kalimdor.",["al"]={"why is delgren in ashenvale","why are there humans in ashenvale","delgren mission"},["q"]="Why is a human paladin all the way out in Ashenvale?"},{["a"]="Delgren and his companions monitor the corrupt activities radiating from the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He directs adventurers to investigate the ruin, hunt the Cult of the Dark Strand, and dismantle their dark summoning practices.",["al"]={"delgren althalaxx","tower of althalaxx quests","cult of the dark strand"},["q"]="What is Delgren's connection to the Tower of Althalaxx?"},{["a"]="Delgren learned Orcish to better comprehend the situation and inhabitants of Kalimdor, a decision that earned him notable disapproval from his superiors within the order.",["al"]={"delgren speaks orcish","does delgren speak orcish","delgren orc language"},["q"]="Why did Delgren learn Orcish?"},{["a"]="He operates alongside Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, working as a coordinated unit to monitor border threats, handle logistics, and purge shadow cultists along the Ashenvale frontier.",["al"]={"delgren companions","who is at maestras post"},["q"]="Who does Delgren work with at Maestra's Post?"}},["kw"]={"althalaxx","argent dawn","ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","cult of the dark strand","delgren","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},["n"]="Delgren the Purifier",["s"]="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post on the northern edge of Ashenvale. Operating alongside comrades Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, he aids the night elves in cleansing demonic and shadow magic threatening the frontier, with a particular focus on the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Human paladins are a rare sight deep within the ancient forests of Kalimdor, but Delgren the Purifier arrived with a mission. Affiliated with the Argent Dawn, Delgren traveled west with a cadre of holy warriors determined to assist the Alliance's new night elf allies against the lingering evils of demons and undead remnants from the Third War. Stationed near the border of Darkshore and Ashenvale, he maintains a watchful vigil over travelers passing south from Auberdine.",["t"]="A Crusader on the Kaldorei Frontier"},{["b"]="Delgren's immediate crusade pits him directly against the Cult of the Dark Strand, a malevolent cabal operating around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Teaming with the scout Balthule Shadowstrike, Delgren orchestrates strikes into the cult's territory, investigating their dark rituals and sending adventurers to strike down cultists, shatter their summoning focuses, and root out corrupt warlocks who dare traffic with demonic shadow.",["t"]="Purging the Dark Strand"},{["b"]="Despite his fierce devotion to the Holy Light and zealous nickname, Delgren possesses an unusual perspective on Kalimdor's tangled politics. Much to the annoyance and disdain of his conservative superiors, he took the time to learn Orcish. This rare linguistic skill hints at an unconventional mind—one that seeks to understand the enemies and neighbors sharing this untamed continent rather than relying solely on blind dogma.",["t"]="An Unorthodox Mind"}}}}}
t["npc:denalan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,412,27.520.0,36.526.0,25.205.0,44.296.0,41.311.0,42.250.0,27.212.0,52.236.0",["h"]="4c952e",["n"]="Denalan",["s"]="Denalan. Denalan es un consumado herborista y botánico elfo de la noche que cuida de una tranquila parcela junto a la orilla oriental del Lago Al'Ameth. Al abrigo de un modesto toldo, consagra sus días al estudio de la flora de la isla y a buscar remedios botánicos para la extraña corrupción que aqueja a Teldrassil. A menudo recurre a jóvenes aventureros para recolectar muestras, estudiar a los violentos brezomaderas y probar tierras encantadas. Mientras muchos kaldorei se centran en la vigilancia marcial o en los grandes ritos druídicos, Denalan cultiva el paciente y meticuloso oficio de la botánica. Asentado en las serenas orillas orientales del Lago Al'Ameth, ha levantado un modesto campamento de investigación provisto de un toldo de tela, aperos sencillos y ordenadas hileras de jardineras de cultivo. En vez de retirarse a los majestuosos túmulos de Darnassus, prefiere permanecer pegado a la tierra para examinar de primera mano la insólita vegetación que ha brotado tras la plantación del nuevo Árbol del Mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common cause with Denalan's lakeside experiments, as his work directly assists the Cenarion Circle's efforts to trace and purge the taint spreading through Teldrassil's roots.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan exemplifies the kaldorei tradition of botanical study, demonstrating how gathering and cultivating wild plants can diagnose deeper ailments in the natural world.",["race:NightElf"]="Denalan's research at Lake Al'Ameth represents early kaldorei attempts to understand the unexpected flaws and growing pains of their new home, Teldrassil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Denalan is located on the eastern bank of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil, south of Dolanaar. He maintains a small camp with an awning and several cultivated planting beds right near the water's edge.",["al"]={"denalan location","where is denalan","denalan map"},["q"]="Where can I find Denalan?"},{["a"]="Denalan is an herbalist studying the unusual flora of Teldrassil and the aggressive behavior of local woodland spirits. He uses enchanted planter boxes to grow timberling seeds, analyze curious wild plant specimens, and find ways to cleanse corruption seeping into the new World Tree's ecosystem.",["al"]={"what does denalan do","denalan purpose","why is denalan at the lake"},["q"]="What is Denalan researching at his campsite?"},{["a"]="Timberlings are plant-like nature spirits native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Normally peaceful parts of the forest ecology, they have become violent and erratic due to an unnatural corruption spreading through the soil and roots of the World Tree, prompting researchers like Denalan to investigate their seeds.",["al"]={"why are timberlings aggressive","timberling lore","corrupted timberlings"},["q"]="Why are the timberlings attacking people?"},{["a"]="Denalan keeps specially prepared planter beds filled with enchanted earth. He uses them to cultivate wild seeds and strange botanical cuttings, allowing him to safely observe how the forest's flora reacts to purified soil away from wild contaminants.",["al"]={"denalan planter","denalans earth","denalan dirt boxes"},["q"]="What are Denalan's planter boxes used for?"},{["a"]="Denalan has worked closely with fellow herbalists such as Sylvia Whisperbloom and stays in regular communication with druidic researchers and scholars across Teldrassil, including Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.",["al"]={"denalan allies","who does denalan report to"},["q"]="Who does Denalan work with?"},{["a"]="The Moss-twined Heart is a blighted botanical core recovered from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling in Teldrassil. Denalan studies it in his enchanted soil to understand the unnatural sickness twisting the island's plant life.",["al"]={"moss twined heart","moss-twined heart quest","blackmoss heart"},["q"]="What is the Moss-twined Heart that Denalan examines?"}},["kw"]={"blackmoss","botany","denalan","herbalist","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","planter","teldrassil","timberlings"},["n"]="Denalan",["s"]="Denalan is an accomplished night elf herbalist and botanist who tends a quiet lakeside plot along the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth. Working under a simple awning, he devotes his days to studying the island's plant life and seeking botanical remedies for the strange corruption affecting Teldrassil. He frequently enlists young adventurers to gather samples, study violent timberlings, and test enchanted soils.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While many kaldorei focus on martial vigilance or high druidic rites, Denalan pursues the patient, meticulous craft of herbalism. Stationed along the tranquil eastern banks of Lake Al'Ameth, he has established a modest research camp consisting of a cloth awning, simple field tools, and tidy rows of cultivated planter boxes. Rather than retreating to the grand barrows of Darnassus, he prefers to remain close to the loam, directly examining the unusual flora that has sprouted since the planting of the new World Tree.",["t"]="A Botanist at Lake Al'Ameth"},{["b"]="Denalan's research is far more than an academic curiosity; it addresses the growing unrest among Teldrassil's native wildlife. The timberlings, normally docile woodland beings of wood and sprout, have turned increasingly aggressive. Denalan enchants specialized soil to nurse wild seeds in captivity and analyze how malignant forces seep into the root systems. By studying strange specimens like shimmering fronds, glowing fruit, and moss-twined growths, he seeks to isolate whatever dark taint is troubling the forest boughs.",["t"]="Investigating Teldrassil's Blemishes"}}}}}
t["npc:dendrite-starblaze"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,368,27.425.0,18.422.0,26.175.0,40.246.0,42.189.0,38.107.0,54.202.0,44.165.0",["h"]="6d16a8",["n"]="Dendrite Rafagaestelar",["s"]="Dendrite Rafagaestelar. Dendrite Rafagaestelar es un druida elfo de la noche que reside en la aldea sagrada de Amparo de la Noche, en Claro de la Luna. Al servicio del Círculo Cenarion, actúa como un mentor y guía esencial para los druidas noveles, tanto elfos de la noche como tauren. A través de él, los practicantes son convocados a la arboleda sagrada para dominar ritos fundamentales como la purificación de toxinas y la comunión con las formas de la naturaleza. Ubicado en Amparo de la Noche, Dendrite Rafagaestelar representa el espíritu neutral y duradero del Círculo Cenarion. Cuando los druidas novatos aprenden a sintonizar sus espíritus con Teletransporte a: Claro de la Luna, Dendrite se encuentra entre los primeros en darles la bienvenida a su llegada. Une la antigua tradición kaldorei con la senda emergente de los tauren, tratando a todos los que escuchan la llamada de la naturaleza como hermanos bajo las ramas del sagrado refugio.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Dendrite Starblaze is one of your principal guides upon first teleporting to Moonglade, instructing you in curing sickness and pursuing aquatic forms.",["race:NightElf"]="Dendrite preserves the classical rites of Kaldorei nature stewardship, welcoming Kaldorei initiates into the Cenarion order at Nighthaven.",["race:Tauren"]="For Shu'halo druids visiting Moonglade from Mulgore, Dendrite serves as living proof that the Cenarion Circle's bond transcends the feud between the Horde and the Alliance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dendrite Starblaze is a night elf druid and Cenarion Circle mentor located in Nighthaven within Moonglade. He guides developing druids through vital class trials and training.",["al"]={"dendrite starblaze","who is dendrite","starblaze moonglade"},["q"]="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?"},{["a"]="The Cenarion Circle stands outside the political factions of the Alliance and Horde. In Moonglade, night elves and tauren practice the druidic arts together under ancient oaths of brotherhood, leaving worldly conflicts beyond the mountain passes.",["al"]={"why does dendrite train horde","dendrite tauren druid","cross faction druid mentor"},["q"]="Why does a night elf train Horde tauren?"},{["a"]="Dendrite oversees several foundational druid class trials. These include quests to master venom and disease curing, as well as trials leading toward the communion required for aquatic form.",["al"]={"dendrite quests","starblaze quest list"},["q"]="What quests does Dendrite Starblaze offer?"},{["a"]="He is located in Nighthaven, the settlement situated on the northern shores of Lake Elune'ara in Moonglade.",["al"]={"dendrite location","where is starblaze","dendrite starblaze map"},["q"]="Where can Dendrite Starblaze be found?"},{["a"]="Novice druids are taught the spell Teleport: Moonglade by their racial trainers around their tenth circle of training. Casting this sends them directly to Moonglade, where Dendrite awaits their arrival.",["al"]={"how to get to dendrite","teleport to moonglade quest"},["q"]="How do young druids reach Dendrite for the first time?"},{["a"]="Non-druids can visit Nighthaven and speak with Dendrite, but he does not offer training, trials, or quests to those outside the Cenarion Circle's druidic traditions.",["al"]={"non druid dendrite","can warrior talk to starblaze"},["q"]="Can non-druid adventurers interact with him?"}},["kw"]={"aquatic form","cenarion circle","curing the sick","dendrite starblaze","druid","lessons anew","moonglade","night elf","nighthaven"},["n"]="Dendrite Starblaze",["s"]="Dendrite Starblaze is a night elf druid residing in the sacred village of Nighthaven within Moonglade. Serving the Cenarion Circle, he acts as a vital mentor and guide for budding druids of both night elf and tauren descent. Through him, practitioners are summoned to the holy grove to master essential rites such as cleansing toxins and communing with nature's forms.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched within Nighthaven, Dendrite Starblaze represents the nonpartisan, enduring spirit of the Cenarion Circle. When novice druids learn to attune their spirits to Teleport: Moonglade, Dendrite is among the first to welcome them upon arrival. He bridges the gap between ancient Kaldorei tradition and the emerging path of the tauren, treating all who heed the call of the wild as kin beneath the boughs of the sacred haven.",["t"]="A Guide in the Sacred Haven"},{["b"]="Dendrite's primary duty involves initiating druidic apprentices into the deeper mysteries of nature. He directs novices through the trials required to understand poison and pestilence, sending them to examine tainted waters and discover herbal curatives. He also oversees the steps that lead druids to the water trials, testing their patience and endurance beneath the surface before granting communion with aquatic forms.",["t"]="Trials of the Wild"}}}}}
t["npc:devrak"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,381,31.509.0,43.382.0,14.350.0,40.258.0,24.282.0,30.189.0,61.189.0,60.262.0,34.211.0",["h"]="f39760",["n"]="Devrak",["s"]="Devrak. Devrak es un maestro de jinetes del viento orco apostado en El Cruce, en Los Baldíos. Como enlace aéreo principal de Kalimdor central, supervisa la red de dracoleones de la Horda que transporta suministros y mensajeros entre Durotar, Mulgore y los puestos de avanzada fronterizos. También se asegura de que la logística crucial, como las carnes de caza y los cueros preparados, llegue sin problemas a las capitales de la Horda. Situado en la intersección de las principales rutas comerciales de Kalimdor, Devrak cuida de los dracoleones que mantienen unida a la Horda a través de vastas distancias. El Cruce se encuentra a la intemperie bajo un sol abrasador, vulnerable tanto a los jabaespines como a los centauros y a los exploradores de la Alianza, lo que hace indispensable el tránsito aéreo rápido. Devrak atiende tanto a caminantes experimentados como a mensajeros novatos, asignando a cada viajero un dracoleón adiestrado capaces de cruzar la sabana y alcanzar las alturas montañosas de Mulgore o los cañones rocosos de Durotar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Devrak is an indispensable ally for any Horde adventurer navigating Kalimdor, serving as the central hub connecting the territories of the orcs, trolls, and tauren.",["race:Orc"]="Stationed in the dry heart of the Barrens, Devrak demonstrates the orcish talent for working with Kalimdor's wind riders, bonding with the fierce beasts to secure aerial dominance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Devrak is the Horde flight master stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He tends the outpost's wind riders, granting flight paths to connecting settlements across Kalimdor and coordinating the transport of couriers, soldiers, and essential trade goods.",["al"]={"who is devrak","what does devrak do","devrak job","crossroads flight master"},["q"]="What is Devrak's role at the Crossroads?"},{["a"]="From his roost at the Crossroads, Devrak connects to major capitals like Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff, as well as frontier outposts in Ashenvale, Stonetalon Mountains, Dustwallow Marsh, Thousand Needles, and southern frontiers, assuming you have spoken to those flight masters first.",["al"]={"devrak flight paths","where can i fly from crossroads","crossroads flight routes"},["q"]="Where can Devrak fly me?"},{["a"]="Devrak assists in courier tasks that teach young Horde adventurers how to use the flight network, including sending fresh meat to Gryshka in Orgrimmar and bundles of hides to Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"devrak quests","crossroads flight quest"},["q"]="What quests does Devrak offer?"},{["a"]="Devrak is guarded by his roost. If assaulted by Alliance raiders or hostile beasts, he can summon ferocious enraged wyverns to aid him in combat, driving attackers off with tooth and talon.",["al"]={"can devrak fight","killing devrak","devrak defense"},["q"]="How does Devrak defend himself if the Crossroads is attacked?"},{["a"]="The Barrens is the connective spine of central Kalimdor. Because the Crossroads links Durotar, Mulgore, Ashenvale, and Stonetalon, Devrak's roost allows the Horde to rapidly reposition forces and coordinate supplies without relying on days-long journeys on foot.",["al"]={"why is crossroads flight master important","crossroads location significance"},["q"]="Why is having a flight master at the Crossroads so critical?"},{["a"]="Devrak manages wind riders, also known as wyverns. These draconic, winged predators native to the peaks and mesas of Kalimdor were befriended by the Horde to serve as reliable flying mounts across rough terrain.",["al"]={"what mounts does devrak have","crossroads mounts"},["q"]="What creatures does Devrak handle?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","flight master","orgrimmar","thunder bluff","wind rider","wyvern"},["n"]="Devrak",["s"]="Devrak is an orc wind rider master stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. Serving as the primary aerial conduit of central Kalimdor, he oversees the Horde's network of wyverns shuttling supplies and couriers between Durotar, Mulgore, and frontier outposts. He also ensures that crucial logistics, such as game meats and prepared hides, travel smoothly to the Horde's capitals.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned at the intersection of Kalimdor's major trade routes, Devrak tends the wyverns that keep the Horde unified across vast distances. The Crossroads sits exposed under the baking sun, vulnerable to quillboar, centaur, and Alliance scouts alike, making rapid aerial transit indispensable. Devrak handles both seasoned wayfarers and untested messengers, pairing riders with trained wind riders capable of crossing the savannah and reaching the mountain heights of Mulgore or the stone canyons of Durotar.",["t"]="Keeper of the Crossroads Roosts"},{["b"]="Beyond ferrying travelers, Devrak plays a vital role in frontier logistics. The hunters of the Barrens harvest meat and pelts in abundance, which Devrak helps channel directly to the cooking fires of Orgrimmar and the tanners of Thunder Bluff. By introducing budding couriers to flight masters across the continents, he cements the aerial lifeline that feeds the Horde's heartlands.",["t"]="Supplies for the Warchief and the Chieftain"},{["b"]="Flight masters in contested frontier territories cannot afford to be defenseless. Devrak is far more than a simple beast handler; when the Crossroads falls under attack, he calls upon enraged wyverns to tear into hostile intruders with venomous stingers and talons, making his roost a dangerous target for anyone bold enough to strike the settlement.",["t"]="A Deadly Roost"}}}}}
t["npc:dextren-ward"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,354,25.431.0,23.452.0,21.368.0,20.169.0,36.190.0,28.175.0,41.206.0,32.182.0,42.186.0",["h"]="1149f2",["n"]="Dextren Tutor",["s"]="Dextren Tutor. Dextren Tutor es un infame criminal y profanador de tumbas encerrado en las Mazmorras de Ventormenta. Antes de su captura, se lucró exhumando cadáveres del Cementerio del Cerro del Cuervo de Bosque del Ocaso y entregándoselos al nigromante Morbent Vil. Atrapado ahora en medio del sangriento motín de la prisión, sigue sentenciado a muerte por el consejo de Villa Oscura. Antes de acabar encadenado bajo las calles de Ventormenta, Dextren Tutor dirigía un negocio tan lúgubre como lucrativo en los bosques asfixiados por la niebla de Bosque del Ocaso. El Cementerio del Cerro del Cuervo ya era un lugar de dolor y horror creciente, pero Tutor convirtió sus camposantos en su cantera privada. En lugar de limitarse a buscar baratijas y reliquias enterradas con los difuntos, Tutor comerciaba con carne, desenterrando tumbas recientes para abastecer a los practicantes de artes oscuras locales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Ward's collaboration with necromancers to provide fresh corpses represents an abhorrent offense against the Sanctity of the Light and the peaceful rest of the departed.",["class:Priest"]="The desecration of holy burial ground at Raven Hill makes Ward's fate an imperative of moral and spiritual restitution.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions assisting Darkshire, putting an end to Dextren Ward is an act of justice for the desecrated families of Duskwood and an essential task in reclaiming the rioting Stockade."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dextren Ward is a notorious criminal imprisoned in the Stormwind Stockade. He is an elite human inmate responsible for robbing the dead in Duskwood to fuel dark rituals.",["al"]={"who is dextren ward","dextren ward lore","stockade dextren"},["q"]="Who is Dextren Ward?"},{["a"]="Ward was captured and imprisoned for grave robbing in Duskwood's Raven Hill Cemetery. Instead of stealing valuables, he exhumed fresh corpses to sell directly to the necromancer Morbent Fel.",["al"]={"why was he arrested","dextren ward crime","what did dextren do"},["q"]="Why is Dextren Ward in the Stockade?"},{["a"]="Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wants Ward dead. Millstipe seeks retribution for the desecration of Duskwood's graves and demands Ward's severed hand as proof of his demise.",["al"]={"who wants dextren dead","dextren ward bounty","crime and punishment questgiver"},["q"]="Who wants Dextren Ward dead?"},{["a"]="Ward acted as a corpse supplier for Morbent Fel. By unearthing the freshly buried dead of Raven Hill Cemetery, Ward provided the raw material Fel needed for his necromantic experiments and undead creations.",["al"]={"morbent fel connection","dextren ward morbent fel","who bought the bodies"},["q"]="What is Ward's connection to Morbent Fel?"},{["a"]="He is located inside the Stormwind Stockade, the high-security prison situated in the canals of Stormwind City. He lurks in one of the holding wings during the ongoing prison revolt.",["al"]={"dextren ward location","where is dextren ward","where to find dextren"},["q"]="Where can Dextren Ward be found?"},{["a"]="Councilman Millstipe explicitly asks for Ward's cold, dead hand as irrefutable physical proof that the grave robber can no longer dig up the graves of Duskwood or profit from necromancy.",["al"]={"why sever his hand","dextren ward hand","proof of death dextren"},["q"]="Why does the quest require Dextren's hand?"}},["kw"]={"councilman millstipe","crime and punishment","dextren ward","duskwood","grave robber","morbent fel","raven hill cemetery","stormwind","the stockade"},["n"]="Dextren Ward",["s"]="Dextren Ward is an infamous criminal and grave robber locked away inside the Stormwind Stockade. Before his capture, he profited by exhuming bodies from Duskwood's Raven Hill Cemetery and delivering them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Now caught in the midst of the prison's bloody uprising, he remains marked for death by the town council of Darkshire.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before ending up in chains beneath the streets of Stormwind, Dextren Ward conducted a grim and lucrative business in the fog-choked woods of Duskwood. Raven Hill Cemetery was already a site of sorrow and growing horror, but Ward treated its burial grounds as a private quarry. Rather than hunting merely for trinkets and heirlooms left with the dead, Ward dealt in flesh, unearthing fresh graves to supply local dark practitioners.",["t"]="Grave Robbery in Duskwood"},{["b"]="Ward's primary customer was Morbent Fel, a necromancer whose dark rituals have plagued Duskwood and swelled the ranks of the undead. In supplying bodies to Fel, Ward actively contributed to the terror that grips Darkshire. Though eventually caught by Stormwind authorities and dragged into the Stockade, his crimes earned him the undying enmity of the people of Duskwood, prompting Councilman Millstipe to demand Ward's hand as proof of justice served.",["t"]="Pawn of the Necromancer"},{["b"]="When a sweeping rebellion broke out inside the Stockade, Ward was not liberated by allies, but rather freed from his cell to join the chaos within the locked-down dungeon. Armed and vicious, he commands his own corner of the prison and uses terror to ward off interlopers, making him one of the priority targets Alliance forces seek to eliminate while restoring order.",["t"]="Chaos in the Stockade"}}}}}
t["npc:dirania-silvershine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,222,23.348.0,16.388.0,27.209.0,37.119.0,42.211.0,31.194.0,51.221.0,51.217.0",["h"]="e5ec90",["n"]="Dirania Brillargente",["s"]="Dirania Brillargente. Dirania Brillargente es una elfa de la noche que reside en Cañada Umbría, en Teldrassil. Profundamente leal y observadora, vela por la apacible arboleda y cuida de su compañero Iverron cuando sus imprudentes andanzas lo ponen en peligro. Dirania permanece entre las tranquilas ramas de Cañada Umbría, el aislado valle donde los jóvenes elfos de la noche comienzan su servicio a Kalimdor y a la Alianza. Mientras muchos en los túmulos y santuarios se centran en amplios deberes espirituales, Dirania permanece atenta a quienes tiene más cerca, pendiente de los peligros silenciosos que se agitan incluso en el corazón de Teldrassil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves stepping into Shadowglen, Dirania serves as an early reminder of the bonds of friendship and the creeping dangers threatening even the newest sanctuaries of the World Tree."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf found in Shadowglen on Teldrassil. She acts as a quest giver, primarily concerned with rescuing and curing her friend Iverron after he runs afoul of local poisonous wildlife.",["al"]={"dirania","who is dirania","dirania silvershine lore"},["q"]="Who is Dirania Silvershine?"},{["a"]="Dirania is located within Shadowglen, the starter vale inside Teldrassil, not far from the central path near Aldrassil.",["al"]={"dirania location","where is dirania","find dirania silvershine"},["q"]="Where can I find Dirania Silvershine?"},{["a"]="Dirania and Iverron are close friends. Dirania is the more sensible and watchful of the pair, stepping in to arrange an antidote whenever Iverron acts foolishly and suffers a poisonous bite from the local fauna.",["al"]={"is dirania related to iverron","iverron and dirania","dirania's friend"},["q"]="What is Dirania's relationship to Iverron?"},{["a"]="She offers quests centered on helping her companion, notably 'A Friend in Need' and 'Iverron's Antidote', tasking adventurers with securing ingredients to brew a cure for Iverron's spider venom.",["al"]={"dirania quests","quests from dirania silvershine","iverron quest"},["q"]="What quests does Dirania offer?"},{["a"]="The webwood spiders dwelling in the boughs of Shadowglen carry a potent venom. While experienced sentinels can handle them, novice elves like Iverron frequently underestimate the danger and risk succumbing to their bites.",["al"]={"shadowglen spiders","why spiders in teldrassil","webwood danger"},["q"]="Why is Dirania worried about spiders in Shadowglen?"},{["a"]="Dirania is an Alliance night elf living peacefully in Teldrassil. She is not depicted as an active member of the Sisterhood of Elune or the Cenarion Circle, but rather a caring civilian looking out for her fellow kin.",["al"]={"dirania faction","is dirania a druid","is dirania a sentinel"},["q"]="Does Dirania belong to any formal order or faction?"}},["kw"]={"antidote","dirania","iverron","shadowglen","silvershine","teldrassil","webwood"},["n"]="Dirania Silvershine",["s"]="Dirania Silvershine is a night elf resident of Shadowglen in Teldrassil. Deeply loyal and observant, she watches over the tranquil grove and looks out for her companion Iverron when his reckless ventures land him in peril.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Dirania stands among the tranquil boughs of Shadowglen, the secluded vale where young night elves begin their service to Kalimdor and the Alliance. While many in the barrow mounds and sanctuaries look to broad spiritual duties, Dirania stays mindful of those nearest to her, attentive to the quiet dangers that stir even in the heart of Teldrassil.",["t"]="A Watcher in Shadowglen"},{["b"]="Dirania's immediate concern is her companion Iverron. Overeager and careless around the poisonous woodland creatures creeping across the glen, Iverron frequently gets into trouble. When he succumbs to a venomous bite from the local webwood spiders, Dirania takes it upon herself to seek out willing hands to gather ingredients and prepare a remedy before the venom takes a permanent toll.",["t"]="A Friend's Peril"}}}}}
t["npc:dorn-plainstalker"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,395,25.386.0,15.401.0,25.212.0,35.215.0,37.210.0,26.152.0,35.237.0,38.171.0",["h"]="fd46e7",["n"]="Dorn Acechaprados",["s"]="Dorn Acechaprados. Dorn Acechaprados es un solitario anciano tauren que reside en El Hueco Perdido, con vistas a los cañones de Las Mil Agujas. Ejerce como supervisor de las tradicionales pruebas del rito de iniciación, desafiando a los aventureros de la Horda a demostrar su carácter y fortaleza. A través de pruebas de fe, resistencia, fuerza y conocimiento, evalúa si los viajeros son dignos servidores de la Madre Tierra y de su pueblo. Aislado en una cueva poco profunda en lo alto de las crestas del cañón de El Hueco Perdido, Dorn Acechaprados vive apartado del bullicio de Poblado Viento Libre. Para llegar a su reducto montañoso es necesario serpentear a lo largo de los escarpados acantilados del norte que dominan las imponentes mesetas situadas abajo. Desde este tranquilo mirador, Dorn mantiene antiguas costumbres y juzga a quienes buscan orientación en los áridos territorios del sur.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Dorn welcomes all Horde champions willing to brave his trials, ensuring that warriors, hunters, and shamans of every race prove their mettle in Kalimdor's rugged wilds.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren wandering through Thousand Needles, Dorn represents the continuation of nomadic ancestral traditions and spiritual rites that test one's balance with the Earth Mother."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dorn Plainstalker is a tauren hermit and elder who dwells in the Weathered Nook, a secluded cliffside shelter high above Thousand Needles. He administers traditional trials of passage to aspiring Horde champions.",["al"]={"who is dorn","dorn lore","dorn plainstalker"},["q"]="Who is Dorn Plainstalker?"},{["a"]="He is located in a cave at the Weathered Nook. From Freewind Post, head north to the high cliff walls bordering the canyon, then follow the ridge east until you discover a ramp ascending into his mountain sanctuary.",["al"]={"where is dorn","how to reach dorn plainstalker","weathered nook location"},["q"]="Where can I find Dorn Plainstalker?"},{["a"]="Dorn oversees four sacred tests: the Test of Faith, Test of Endurance, Test of Strength, and Test of Lore. Completing them proves a traveler's courage, physical resolve, combat skill, and respect for tradition.",["al"]={"dorn plainstalker quests","test of faith","trials of passage thousand needles"},["q"]="What are the trials Dorn administers?"},{["a"]="The Test of Faith requires the pilgrim to step off a dizzying cliff plank into the chasm below, demonstrating absolute trust and overcoming primal fear.",["al"]={"leap of faith thousand needles","test of faith dorn"},["q"]="What is the Test of Faith?"},{["a"]="Dorn adheres to ascetic tauren spiritual traditions. By dwelling alone in the heights of the Weathered Nook, away from the daily trade and defense of Freewind Post, he maintains an untroubled place of contemplation and trial for seekers.",["al"]={"why is dorn isolated","dorn plainstalker background"},["q"]="Why does Dorn live alone in a cave?"},{["a"]="While he lives outside Freewind Post itself, Dorn is a loyal member of the Horde and the tauren tribes, assisting brave travelers who wander through the windswept canyons.",["al"]={"freewind post elder","is dorn horde"},["q"]="Is Dorn affiliated with Freewind Post?"}},["kw"]={"dorn plainstalker","freewind post","tauren trial","test of endurance","test of faith","test of lore","test of strength","thousand needles","weathered nook"},["n"]="Dorn Plainstalker",["s"]="Dorn Plainstalker is a solitary tauren elder residing in the Weathered Nook overlooking the canyons of Thousand Needles. He serves as an overseer of traditional rite of passage trials, challenging Horde adventurers to prove their character and fortitude. Through trials of faith, endurance, strength, and lore, he tests whether travelers are worthy servants of the Earth Mother and their people.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Secluded in a shallow cave high atop the canyon ridges of the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker lives apart from the bustle of Freewind Post. Reaching his mountain redoubt requires winding along the sheer northern cliffs overlooking the towering mesas below. From this quiet vantage point, Dorn maintains ancient customs and judges those who seek guidance in the harsh southern barrens.",["t"]="Hermit of the High Cliffs"},{["b"]="Dorn Plainstalker guides pilgrims through a demanding series of tests meant to measure the core virtues of a tauren champion: faith, endurance, strength, and lore. Rather than mere exercises in brute force, these trials force aspirants to confront fear, leap blindly into the unknown, outlast cunning wilderness predators, and ponder the sacred history of Kalimdor before claiming their final passage.",["t"]="The Four Trials"}}}}}
t["npc:duthorian-rall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,388,27.502.0,29.469.0,18.450.1,22.257.0,34.135.0,47.216.0,45.216.0,66.235.0,45.144.0",["h"]="9c7606",["n"]="Duthorian Rall",["s"]="Duthorian Rall. Duthorian Rall es un respetado caballero humano de la Mano de Plata apostado en la Catedral de la Luz de Ventormenta. Reconocido como uno de los paladines más influyentes de la Alianza, supervisa el entrenamiento y las pruebas espirituales de los guerreros sagrados emergentes. Guía a los reclutas a través de votos solemnes de caridad, valor y devoción para defender Azeroth contra la Plaga y las amenazas internas al acecho. Situado en el transepto abovedado de la Catedral de la Luz, Duthorian Rall representa las venerables tradiciones de los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata. Con el reino inquieto por los conflictos internos y la desaparición del rey Varian Wrynn, Duthorian asume el vital deber de inculcar una disciplina recta en los nuevos iniciados. Paladines respetados en el campo de batalla, incluidos Hermano Fijalontad en Villanorte y Brandur Martiyerro en Forjaz, dirigen a los reclutas prometedores a su tutela para comenzar sus pruebas sagradas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Duthorian Rall is one of your primary spiritual mentors in Stormwind, testing your compassion and valor through foundational trials that unlock the power of resurrection, divine senses, and your warhorse.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an influential leader within the Silver Hand, Duthorian ensures that the Alliance's defenders remain morally upright and capable of defending the realm against bandits and undead alike.",["race:Human"]="Anchored in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, Duthorian represents the enduring devotion and chivalric discipline central to human faith and society."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Duthorian Rall is a prominent knight of the Silver Hand residing in the Cathedral of Light within Stormwind City. He serves as an instructor and spiritual mentor for new paladins, testing their devotion and courage on behalf of the Church of the Holy Light.",["al"]={"duthorian rall lore","who is duthorian","cathedral paladin duthorian"},["q"]="Who is Duthorian Rall?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing in the eastern wing of the Cathedral of Light, located at the heart of the Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",["al"]={"where is duthorian rall","duthorian rall location","how to find duthorian"},["q"]="Where can Duthorian Rall be found?"},{["a"]="Duthorian provides paladins with the Book of Divinity and guides them through trials of humility, compassion, and rescue. Fulfilling his trials proves an initiate is worthy to wield the Light's power of resurrection.",["al"]={"tome of divinity duthorian","redemption quest duthorian","symbol of life quest"},["q"]="What is his connection to the Tome of Divinity?"},{["a"]="During the trial for the Tome of Valor, Duthorian sends paladins to protect Daphne Stilwell from Defias bandits on her farm in Westfall, demonstrating their willingness to sacrifice themselves to defend the innocent.",["al"]={"daphne stilwell quest","tome of valor westfall","westfall paladin quest"},["q"]="Why does Duthorian send paladins to Westfall?"},{["a"]="Successful paladins earn key holy capabilities through his guidance, including the sacred gift of resurrection, the ability to sense undead, protective armaments such as the Bastion of Stormwind, and eventually their summoned warhorse.",["al"]={"duthorian quest rewards","what do you get from duthorian"},["q"]="What rewards does Duthorian grant to paladins who pass his trials?"},{["a"]="Aspirants are typically directed to him by paladin trainers, including Brother Wilhelm in Northshire Valley and Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge.",["al"]={"who sends you to duthorian","duthorian breadcrumb quest"},["q"]="Who sends adventurers to Duthorian initially?"}},["kw"]={"cathedral of light","daphne stilwell","duthorian rall","jordan stilwell","paladin trainer","silver hand","stormwind","symbol of life","tome of divinity","tome of valor"},["n"]="Duthorian Rall",["s"]="Duthorian Rall is a respected human knight of the Silver Hand stationed within Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Renowned as one of the most influential paladins in the Alliance, he oversees the training and spiritual trials of emerging holy warriors. He guides recruits through solemn vows of charity, valor, and devotion to defend Azeroth against the Scourge and lurking domestic threats.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing within the vaulted transept of the Cathedral of Light, Duthorian Rall represents the venerable traditions of the Knights of the Silver Hand. With the kingdom unsettled by internal strife and the missing King Varian Wrynn, Duthorian shoulders the vital duty of instilling righteous discipline in fresh initiates. Respected paladins in the field, including Brother Wilhelm in Northshire and Brandur Ironhammer in Ironforge, direct promising recruits to his guidance to begin their sacred trials.",["t"]="A Pillar of the Silver Hand"},{["b"]="Duthorian teaches that martial power without moral foundation is hollow. Through the Tome of Divinity, he tests a paladin's capacity for empathy, requiring acts of mercy and selfless service across Stormwind before entrusting them with deeper mysteries. His trials culminate in testing candidates with the Symbol of Life near Heroes' Vigil, sending them to aid wounded allies and teach them to channel the Light's miraculous power to restore fallen comrades from death.",["t"]="Trials of Compassion and Life"},{["b"]="Beyond spiritual contemplation, Duthorian demands resolute courage in the face of peril. In his tests of valor, he cautions aspirants that their vows may demand their lives. He tests this resolve by sending initiates into dangerous territory—such as defending Daphne Stilwell against Defias renegades in Westfall—before directing them on toward master smith Jordan Stilwell outside Ironforge and granting them holy steeds worthy of their station.",["t"]="The Price of Valor"}}}}}
t["npc:edwin-vancleef"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,354,24.539.0,28.580.0,28.533.1,22.202.0,49.258.0,31.164.1,39.205.0,46.246.0,37.169.1",["h"]="92dfbc",["n"]="Edwin VanCleef",["s"]="Edwin VanCleef. Edwin VanCleef fue el brillante maestre del gremio de los Albañiles que reconstruyó Ciudad de Ventormenta tras la Segunda Guerra. Tras ser estafado por la Casa de los Nobles, que le denegó el pago, lideró una violenta revuelta obrera y formó la ilegal Hermandad Defias. Al operar desde las profundidades de Las Minas de la Muerte en Páramos de Poniente, busca venganza contra el reino que ayudó a restaurar. Tras la devastación de la Primera Guerra, Edwin VanCleef fue elegido para liderar al gremio de los Albañiles en la monumental tarea de reconstruir Ciudad de Ventormenta. Artesano sin igual e idealista, VanCleef dirigió la construcción de las imponentes murallas y las altas catedrales de la capital, e incluso supervisó el levantamiento del Castillo de Nethergarde para vigilar El Portal Oscuro. Junto a su maestría en la arquitectura, VanCleef era un agente extraordinariamente letal; fue entrenado en el sigilo, el subterfugio y el manejo de las hojas por su amigo de la infancia, Mathias Shaw.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef was trained by SI:7 leader Mathias Shaw himself, making him one of the most capable rogues in Azeroth, blending formal guild leadership with elite assassination techniques.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance commanders consider VanCleef the premier internal security threat to southern human lands, paralyzing Westfall and the borders of Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, VanCleef embodies the tragedy of the kingdom's postwar recovery: a loyal hero whose denied livelihood turned him into the realm's deadliest insurgent."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is the mastermind behind the Defias Brotherhood and the former Guildmaster of the Stonemasons. He is the master architect who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Horde destroyed it during the First War.",["al"]={"who is vancleef","edwin vancleef lore","vancleef identity"},["q"]="Who is Edwin VanCleef?"},{["a"]="After the rebuilding of Stormwind City, the House of Nobles refused to pay the Stonemasons Guild their agreed wages due to excessive kingdom debt. When VanCleef and the workers protested, the nobles disbanded the guild, igniting violent riots in the streets.",["al"]={"why did defias rebel","why did stonemasons riot","reason for defias riot"},["q"]="Why did the Stonemasons revolt against Stormwind?"},{["a"]="He commands the Defias Brotherhood from the innermost sanctum of the Deadmines in Westfall, whose entrance is rumored to lie through the quiet village of Moonbrook.",["al"]={"where is vancleef","vancleef location","deadmines boss location"},["q"]="Where is Edwin VanCleef hiding?"},{["a"]="Mathias Shaw was a childhood friend of Edwin. Shaw personally trained VanCleef in the arts of stealth, thievery, and combat, originally hoping VanCleef would join him in the royal intelligence agency SI:7.",["al"]={"vancleef and shaw","is vancleef related to shaw","mathias shaw friend"},["q"]="What is his connection to Mathias Shaw?"},{["a"]="During the chaotic street riots stirred by the unpaid Stonemasons, a hurled stone struck and killed King Varian's young wife, Queen Tiffin Wrynn. Her death drove King Varian into a furious crackdown, forcing VanCleef and his men to flee the city.",["al"]={"how did tiffin die","who killed tiffin wrynn","queen tiffin death"},["q"]="What happened to Queen Tiffin during the riot?"},{["a"]="Rumor has it that the Defias have conscripted clever goblins to help them build something terrible at the bottom of the Deadmines, but what it may be is still uncertain.",["al"]={"deadmines ship","what is inside deadmines","vancleef warship"},["q"]="What is he building in the Deadmines?"}},["kw"]={"brotherhood","deadmines","defias","moonbrook","stonemasons","stormwind","vancleef","westfall"},["n"]="Edwin VanCleef",["s"]="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant Guildmaster of the Stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second War. After being cheated of payment by the House of Nobles, he led a violent workers' revolt and formed the outlaw Defias Brotherhood. Operating from deep within the Deadmines of Westfall, he seeks vengeance against the kingdom he helped restore.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the devastation of the First War, Edwin VanCleef was chosen to lead the Stonemasons Guild in the monumental task of rebuilding Stormwind City. A peerless craftsman and an idealist, VanCleef directed the construction of the capital's grand ramparts and towering cathedrals, and even oversaw the erection of Nethergarde Keep to watch over the Dark Portal. Alongside his mastery of architecture, VanCleef was a remarkably deadly operative; he was trained in stealth, subterfuge, and bladecraft by his childhood friend, Mathias Shaw.",["t"]="Architect of the Kingdom"},{["b"]="When the years of labor concluded, the House of Nobles ran up colossal debts through military campaigns and refused to provide the Stonemasons their promised compensation. Enraged, VanCleef demanded restitution, only for the nobles to officially dissolve the guild. The artisans revolted, triggering chaotic street riots in Stormwind during which King Varian Wrynn's wife, Queen Tiffin, was slain. Driven out of the capital by the crown's retribution, VanCleef gathered his exiled workers and allied outcasts in Westfall, uniting them beneath the banner of the Defias Brotherhood.",["t"]="The Riot and the Brotherhood"},{["b"]="Taking advantage of the crown's neglect of the countryside, the Defias drove off Westfall's farmers and claimed its rich gold deposits. Within the depths of Moonbrook's Deadmines, VanCleef oversaw the construction of a massive juggernaut warship, preparing an armed assault against Stormwind itself. While the House of Nobles dismissed the thieves as disorganized brigands, VanCleef forged alliances with river crooks, gnolls, and the Bloodsail Buccaneers, turning an embittered labor union into an army poised to crush the monarchy.",["t"]="Retribution from the Shadows"}}}}}
t["npc:eitrigg"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,404,26.720.0,15.714.0,25.608.0,15.245.0,46.363.0,33.208.0,36.302.0,36.259.0,51.139.0",["h"]="d22302",["n"]="Eitrigg",["s"]="Eitrigg. Eitrigg es un curtido veterano de la Primera y Segunda Guerra que permanece junto al Jefe de Guerra Thrall como un estimado consejero en Orgrimmar. Antaño un teniente de alto rango del Clan Roca Negra, acabó desilusionado con la vieja Horda demoníaca y vivió en el exilio hasta que una extraordinaria amistad con un paladín humano cambió su destino. En la actualidad, ayuda a guiar a la nueva Horda de regreso a sus raíces de honor y chamanismo. Nacido en Draenor en el seno del Clan Roca Negra, Eitrigg fue antaño uno de los principales tenientes del Jefe de Guerra Puño Negro junto a Orgrim Martillo Maldito y Varok Colmillosauro. Cuando Martillo Maldito se hizo con el liderazgo de la Horda, Eitrigg siguió siendo un oficial de confianza y custodió a la prisionera semiorca y asesina Garona. Aunque al principio desestimó las revelaciones de ella sobre Gul'dan y la corrupción demoníaca del Consejo de la Sombra, las espantosas batallas y la derrota definitiva de la Horda en la Segunda Guerra lo obligaron a afrontar la oscura realidad. Asqueado al darse cuenta de cómo habían manipulado a su pueblo, Eitrigg se apartó de los remanentes dispersos y se retiró a un exilio autoimpuesto, buscando únicamente la soledad en las tierras salvajes de Lordaeron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="The story of Eitrigg and Tirion Fordring is renowned among paladins as the ultimate test of duty versus righteous honor.",["class:Warrior"]="Eitrigg represents martial honor preserved through decades of tragedy, having survived two wars through sheer strength and unbroken discipline.",["faction:Horde"]="Eitrigg serves as the living institutional memory of the Horde, standing by Thrall to ensure the mistakes of the demon-tainted past are never repeated.",["race:Orc"]="For the orcs of Durotar, Eitrigg is a revered elder whose Blackrock heritage proves that any orc can embrace honor and redeem their people's legacy."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Eitrigg is an elderly Blackrock orc warrior who served as a lieutenant under Blackhand and Orgrim Doomhammer during the First and Second Wars. Today, he resides in Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar as a trusted counselor and advisor to Warchief Thrall.",["al"]={"who is eitrigg","eitrigg lore","orc standing by thrall"},["q"]="Who is Eitrigg?"},{["a"]="While living in exile in Lordaeron, Eitrigg saved the life of the paladin Tirion Fordring during a duel that brought down a stone tower. In return, Tirion defended Eitrigg's location and later fought his own people in Stratholme to prevent Eitrigg's execution, losing his title and lands in the process. Bound by mutual honor, Eitrigg views Tirion as his brother.",["al"]={"eitrigg and tirion","eitrigg human friend","blood and honor"},["q"]="Why does Eitrigg consider a human his brother?"},{["a"]="Eitrigg belongs to the Blackrock clan. He was a high-ranking commander during the old wars, though he abandoned the clan's corrupt remnants after learning the truth of the demonic corruption that guided them.",["al"]={"eitrigg clan","is eitrigg blackrock"},["q"]="What clan does Eitrigg belong to?"},{["a"]="During the Second War, Eitrigg guarded the assassin Garona, who revealed the demon worship and manipulations of Gul'dan and the Shadow Council. Following the Horde's defeat, Eitrigg realized her claims were true and left in disgust, seeking a quiet place to die rather than serve a corrupt war machine.",["al"]={"why did eitrigg leave","eitrigg exile"},["q"]="Why did Eitrigg leave the old Horde?"},{["a"]="When Alliance forces captured Eitrigg and prepared to execute him in Stratholme, Thrall and his forces raided the city and freed him. Seeing Thrall's commitment to honor and the rediscovery of shamanism, Eitrigg chose to follow the young Warchief to Kalimdor.",["al"]={"how did eitrigg meet thrall","eitrigg rescued"},["q"]="How did Eitrigg end up in Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="Eitrigg advises Thrall directly within Grommash Hold and assists in testing and evaluating new recruits who swear loyalty to the New Horde.",["al"]={"eitrigg quest","what does eitrigg do"},["q"]="What role does Eitrigg play in Orgrimmar right now?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock clan","blood and honor","eitrigg","grommash hold","hearthglen","orgrim doomhammer","orgrimmar","stratholme","thrall","tirion fordring"},["n"]="Eitrigg",["s"]="Eitrigg is a seasoned veteran of the First and Second Wars who stands beside Warchief Thrall as an esteemed advisor in Orgrimmar. Once a high-ranking lieutenant of the Blackrock clan, he became disillusioned with the old demonic Horde and lived in exile until an extraordinary friendship with a human paladin changed his fate. Today, he helps guide the New Horde back to its roots of honor and shamanism.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Born on Draenor into the Blackrock clan, Eitrigg was once one of Warchief Blackhand's primary lieutenants alongside Orgrim Doomhammer and Varok Saurfang. When Doomhammer seized leadership of the Horde, Eitrigg remained a trusted officer and oversaw the captured half-orc assassin Garona. Although he initially dismissed her revelations regarding Gul'dan and the demonic corruption of the Shadow Council, the horrific battles and ultimate defeat of the Horde in the Second War forced him to confront the dark reality. Sickened by the realization of how his people had been manipulated, Eitrigg walked away from the scattered remnants and retreated into self-imposed exile, seeking only solitude in the wilds of Lordaeron.",["t"]="A Veteran of the Old Horde"},{["b"]="Years into his wilderness exile, Eitrigg was discovered sheltering in an abandoned tower near Hearthglen by the human paladin Tirion Fordring. Their initial clash collapsed the ruins, but instead of finishing the unconscious human, Eitrigg pulled him from the rubble to safety. Moved by this display of pure martial honor, Tirion swore an oath of friendship and refused to betray the hermit's location. When the local Alliance authorities ultimately captured Eitrigg and sentenced him to hang in Stratholme, Tirion threw away his own knighthood, lands, and freedom in an attack to rescue the condemned orc. This legendary bond proved to both warriors that honor transcended the bitter hatred between their species.",["t"]="Blood and Honor"},{["b"]="During Tirion's desperate attempt to free Eitrigg in Stratholme, Thrall's newly united Horde raided the city and extracted the aging warrior. Meeting Thrall convinced Eitrigg that the orcs were throwing off the demonic taint and rediscovering their ancestral shamanic heritage. Returning with Thrall across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, Eitrigg took up a revered post in the Valley of Wisdom within Orgrimmar. He now stands inside Grommash Hold as an advisor to the young Warchief, helping evaluate new recruits and imparting his hard-earned wisdom so that the New Horde never repeats the tragedies of the past.",["t"]="Counselor to the Warchief"}}}}}
t["npc:electrocutioner-6000"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,310,32.492.0,24.433.0,44.135.0,36.234.0,31.294.0,66.206.0,49.171.0",["h"]="5b14c5",["n"]="Electrocutor 6000",["s"]="Electrocutor 6000. El Electrocutor 6000 es un letal y sobrecargado tanque araña desplegado para defender la Hangar de Lanzamiento en las salas irradiadas de Gnomeregan. Pilotado por el infame gnomo paria, el teniente Tom «Chisporroteo» Manivela, representa la temeraria ambición del Mekigeniero Termochufe de utilizar la electricidad de alto voltaje como arma. El Mekigeniero Termochufe nunca ha destacado por realizar rigurosas pruebas de seguridad. Impulsado por la megalomanía y las prisas, suele enviar máquinas de guerra no probadas directamente de la mesa de dibujo al combate real. El Electrocutor 6000 fue su intento inicial de aprovechar las corrientes eléctricas puras como un sistema ofensivo montado sobre el chasis blindado de un tanque araña. En lugar de resolver las sobrecargas eléctricas letales en un laboratorio, Termochufe lo envió de inmediato a vigilar los niveles superiores de la Hangar de Lanzamiento de Gnomeregan.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Breaching the Launch Bay and eliminating Crankle is vital to securing the Workshop Key, bypassing hazardous front corridors during liberation efforts into Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers marvel at the raw high-voltage output harnessed within the chassis, even if Thermaplugg's reckless lack of grounding makes it a lethal hazard to its own crew.",["race:Gnome"]="For the exiled gnomes of Ironforge, the Electrocutioner 6000 is an insult to their craft: a dangerous, untested monstrosity that reflects Thermaplugg's twisted disregard for proper engineering ethics and gnome lives."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Electrocutioner 6000 is positioned on an elevated catwalk platform overlooking the Launch Bay inside the fallen city of Gnomeregan.",["al"]={"electrocutioner 6000 location","where is electrocutioner","find electrocutioner 6000"},["q"]="Where can the Electrocutioner 6000 be found?"},{["a"]="It is piloted by Lieutenant Tom Crankle, better known as 'Sizzlepants.' He is a crazed leper gnome officer who achieved renown among Thermaplugg's forces as the sole pilot to survive the tank's dangerous internal electrical discharge.",["al"]={"who drives electrocutioner 6000","sizzlepants","tom sizzlepants crankle","pilot of electrocutioner"},["q"]="Who pilots the Electrocutioner 6000?"},{["a"]="Mekgineer Thermaplugg refuses to spend time conducting proper safety evaluations, preferring to rush inventions immediately into service. The Electrocutioner 6000 was his first trial with an electrified spider tank, leaving its lethal power feeds volatile and perilous even to its own operator.",["al"]={"why does it shock","electrocutioner prototype","thermaplugg design"},["q"]="Why is the machine so volatile?"},{["a"]="The pilot holds the Workshop Key, an essential device that unlocks the back door entrance into Gnomeregan's deeper engineering sectors, allowing strike teams a faster route through the reclaimed facilities.",["al"]={"workshop key","why kill electrocutioner","electrocutioner 6000 loot"},["q"]="Why is defeating the Electrocutioner 6000 important for explorers?"},{["a"]="It is a modified spider tank, functioning as an armored mechano-vehicle guided manually by its pilot from an internal cockpit, rather than an autonomous robotic construct.",["al"]={"is electrocutioner a robot","electrocutioner spider tank type"},["q"]="Is the Electrocutioner an automaton or a vehicle?"}},["kw"]={"crankle","electrocutioner","gnomeregan","launch bay","sizzlepants","spider tank","thermaplugg","workshop key"},["n"]="Electrocutioner 6000",["s"]="The Electrocutioner 6000 is a deadly, super-charged spider tank deployed to defend the Launch Bay within the irradiated halls of Gnomeregan. Piloted by the notorious leper gnome Lieutenant Tom 'Sizzlepants' Crankle, it represents Mekgineer Thermaplugg's reckless ambition to weaponize high-voltage electricity.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Mekgineer Thermaplugg has never been known for rigorous safety testing. Driven by megalomania and haste, he regularly rushes unproven war machines straight from the drawing board into live combat. The Electrocutioner 6000 was his initial attempt to harness raw electrical currents as an offensive system mounted to an armored spider tank chassis. Rather than working out lethal power surges in a laboratory, Thermaplugg sent it immediately to guard the upper tiers of Gnomeregan's Launch Bay.",["t"]="Thermaplugg's Shocking Prototype"},{["b"]="Operating experimental machinery is often a death sentence, particularly when lethal voltage is involved. Early test pilots perished in agonizing mishaps, but Lieutenant Tom Crankle managed to withstand the lethal surges and survived at the controls. Earning the grim moniker 'Sizzlepants,' he became an idol of resilience among the irradiated leper gnomes loyal to Thermaplugg, fiercely guarding the path toward the inner workshops.",["t"]="Lieutenant 'Sizzlepants'"}}}}}
t["npc:elling-trias"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,377,23.523.0,17.478.0,20.442.1,20.243.0,33.161.0,49.235.1,30.211.0,27.163.0,62.220.1",["h"]="cb9953",["n"]="Elling Trias",["s"]="Elling Trias. Elling Trias regenta Queso de Trias, un pequeño establecimiento situado en el bullicioso Distrito de Mercaderes de la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Aunque se presenta como un jovial y apasionado vendedor de lácteos, opera discretamente como uno de los intermediarios de información mejor conectados del reino. Entre ruedas de queso y charlas cordiales, Trias mantiene el oído bien atento a todo lo que ocurre a lo largo de varios continentes. Para el cliente casual que pasea por el Distrito de Mercaderes, Elling Trias no es más que un artesano dedicado a los quesos selectos que atiende su negocio junto a su esposa Elaine y su hijo Ben. Promociona con entusiasmo ruedas de queso y charla amistosamente con los lugareños. Sin embargo, quienes están al tanto saben que Queso de Trias es una de las tapaderas más fiables de Ventormenta. El constante ajetreo del comercio urbano ofrece la cobertura perfecta para operativos, cortesanos y aventureros que necesitan intercambiar información discreta sin llamar la atención de la guardia de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Any practitioner of subtlety recognizes that Elling's cheese shop is an ideal drop point. His proximity to Old Town and tight links to Mathias Shaw make him a fixture in Stormwind's underworld.",["faction:Alliance"]="Elling serves as an unsung pillar of Alliance intelligence, quietly filtering rumors from Theramore to Hearthglen to protect the realm from internal rot."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Elling Trias is ostensibly a cheese vendor operating Trias' Cheese in Stormwind's Trade District alongside his family. Beneath that cover, he is a seasoned intelligence broker with ties to SI:7, the Church, and distant outposts across Azeroth.",["al"]={"who is elling","elling trias identity","trias cheese guy"},["q"]="Who is Elling Trias?"},{["a"]="You can find Trias' Cheese in the Trade District of Stormwind City, tucked into the shop row along the outer canal wall, near the border leading toward Old Town.",["al"]={"trias cheese location","where is elling trias","trias shop stormwind"},["q"]="Where is his cheese shop located?"},{["a"]="Trias is not a member of the Defias Brotherhood; rather, he tracks their movements through his informant network. He helps Alliance adventurers trace Defias involvement in subversive plots, including the kidnapping of a royal diplomat.",["al"]={"trias defias","is trias in the defias"},["q"]="What is his connection to the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Elling collaborates closely with Master Mathias Shaw and the intelligence apparatus of SI:7. His shop provides an informal listening post where discreet inquiries can be launched outside official royal channels.",["al"]={"trias and shaw","trias si7","is trias si7"},["q"]="How does he know Mathias Shaw?"},{["a"]="Elling runs Trias' Cheese with his wife, Elaine Trias, and his son, Ben Trias. Together they maintain the appearance of a bustling, ordinary family-run trade shop.",["al"]={"trias family","elling trias wife"},["q"]="Who runs the shop with him?"},{["a"]="Sent to Trias by Bishop DeLavey, investigators use Elling's expansive web of contacts—including his old associates Jorgen and Tyrion—to trace Defias movements and discover who seized the diplomat bound for Theramore.",["al"]={"missing diplomat trias","why visit trias cheese"},["q"]="What is his involvement in the Missing Diplomat investigation?"}},["kw"]={"elaine trias","elling trias","mathias shaw","missing diplomat","si:7","stormwind","trade district","trias cheese","tyrion"},["n"]="Elling Trias",["s"]="Elling Trias manages Trias' Cheese, a small storefront nestled in the bustling Trade District of Stormwind City. While he presents himself as a jovial and passionate purveyor of dairy, he quietly operates as one of the kingdom's most connected information brokers. Behind wheels of cheese and cordial banter, Trias maintains an ear to the ground that reaches across continents.",["sec"]={{["b"]="To the casual customer strolling the Trade District, Elling Trias is merely an artisan dedicated to fine curds, working his shop alongside his wife Elaine and son Ben. He enthusiastically hawks wheels of cheese and chats amicably with townsfolk. Yet those in the know understand that Trias' Cheese is one of the most reliable fronts in Stormwind. The steady hum of city commerce provides perfect cover for operatives, courtiers, and adventurers who need to trade quiet words without drawing the attention of the city watch.",["t"]="The Master Cheesemonger"},{["b"]="Elling's network of informants and allies is staggering for a shopkeeper. He maintains ties with Master Mathias Shaw of SI:7, coordinates with Church contacts like Bishop DeLavey, and corresponds with agents as far afield as Darkshire, Theramore Isle, and the distant Plaguelands near Hearthglen. When odd rumors surface—whether concerning highway bandits or quiet movements in the countryside—Trias often pieces the puzzle together long before the royal court takes notice.",["t"]="A Web of Whispers"},{["b"]="When a high-ranking diplomat vanishes on a voyage to Theramore, Elling Trias becomes an essential pivot in unraveling the conspiracy. Directing investigators to his contacts—including an estranged operative named Jorgen and old friend Tyrion—Trias helps unmask the Defias Brotherhood's hand in the abduction. Despite his sharp wit and cynical banter, Elling recognizes that the plot reaches deep into the heart of Stormwind's aristocracy.",["t"]="The Missing Diplomat"}}}}}
t["npc:executor-arren"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,332,23.510.0,24.454.0,18.435.1,22.220.0,44.211.0,49.217.0,46.218.0,27.196.0,58.189.0",["h"]="0f0b95",["n"]="Ejecutor Arren",["s"]="Ejecutor Arren. El Ejecutor Arren es un oficial Renegado de alto rango apostado en Camposanto. Supervisa la defensa inmediata y la consolidación del asentamiento a medida que los no-muertos recién despertados emergen de sus tumbas. Arren coordina la campaña local contra los zombis descerebrados de la Plaga, las bestias salvajes y los invasores fanáticos de la Cruzada Escarlata. Firme y resuelto justo a las afueras de la capilla de Camposanto, el Ejecutor Arren ejerce como la principal voz militar para los Renegados nacientes dentro de sus terrenos de despertar. Mientras los celadores de las criptas guían a los no-muertos recién alzados a través de su desorientación, Arren dirige su atención hacia el exterior en pos de la supervivencia. Bajo el estandarte de la Reina Sylvanas Brisaveloz, organiza operaciones locales para barrer a los zombis descerebrados que amenazan las fronteras de la aldea, estableciendo un territorio seguro a la sombra de la caída de Lordaeron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Arren's frontline commands in Deathknell represent the Horde's initial foothold in northern Lordaeron, securing survival amidst hostile surroundings.",["race:Undead"]="Executor Arren is one of the first commanders every Forsaken meets upon emerging into Tirisfal, giving them their earliest taste of duty under the Dark Lady."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Executor Arren is the commanding military officer overseeing Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. He organizes newly risen Forsaken into an effective fighting force to defend the village and secure the surrounding countryside.",["al"]={"arren role","who is arren","deathknell executor"},["q"]="Who is Executor Arren?"},{["a"]="Executors are trusted military and administrative commanders within the Forsaken hierarchy. They govern local garrisons, direct operations in the field, and enforce the will and law of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",["al"]={"executor title","what is an executor","forsaken executor rank"},["q"]="What rank is an Executor among the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="The zombies prowling near Deathknell are mindless Scourge remnants left behind after the plague devastated Lordaeron. Arren orders them cleared so that newly awakened undead are not torn apart upon leaving the crypts.",["al"]={"why kill zombies","the damned quest","mindless scourge"},["q"]="Why does Arren send recruits against the zombies?"},{["a"]="The Scarlet Crusade is a radical human faction dedicated to exterminating all undead. They hold outposts across the ruins of Lordaeron and actively seek to purge the Forsaken, considering them identical to the Scourge.",["al"]={"scarlet crusade tirisfal","why crusade here","crusaders in deathknell"},["q"]="Why is the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades?"},{["a"]="Night Web's Hollow is a spider-infested cave north of Deathknell. Arren directs recruits to clear out the aggressive arachnids to eliminate a major local hazard and demonstrate martial competence.",["al"]={"spider cave deathknell","night webs hollow","arren spider quest"},["q"]="What is Night Web's Hollow?"},{["a"]="Once Deathknell's immediate threats are neutralized, Arren directs capable recruits outward to Brill to report to Executor Zygand and aid the broader Forsaken effort across Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"next after deathknell","where to go after arren","the executor in the field"},["q"]="Where does Arren send recruits once they finish his tasks?"}},["kw"]={"deathknell","executor arren","forsaken","night web's hollow","scarlet crusade","sylvanas","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Executor Arren",["s"]="Executor Arren is a high-ranking Forsaken officer stationed in Deathknell. He oversees the immediate defense and consolidation of the settlement as newly awakened undead emerge from their graves. Arren coordinates the local campaign against mindless Scourge zombies, feral beasts, and the encroaching zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing resolute just outside the chapel in Deathknell, Executor Arren serves as the primary military voice for the nascent Forsaken within their awakening grounds. While the caretakers in the crypts guide newly raised undead through their disorientation, Arren directs their focus outward toward survival. Under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's banner, he organizes local operations to sweep away mindless zombies that threaten the village borders, establishing secure territory in the shadow of Lordaeron's fall.",["t"]="Commander of Deathknell"},{["b"]="Deathknell is surrounded by perils far deadlier than confused fledglings. Under Arren's orders, scouts and initiates strike at the vicious arachnids inhabiting Night Web's Hollow and eliminate dangerous predators haunting the woodland fringes. By demanding decisive action from every capable hand, Arren tests the fortitude of new arrivals, ensuring only those capable of defending their second chance at existence remain in the service of the Dark Lady.",["t"]="Securing the Borderlands"},{["b"]="Arren's greatest strategic concern lies with the Scarlet Crusade. The zealots consider all undead to be monstrosities requiring total eradication, failing or refusing to distinguish between the Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. Arren organizes targeted strikes against Scarlet patrols encamped in the Tirisfal wilderness, intercepting couriers and analyzing stolen dispatches to safeguard Deathknell from being purged in holy fire.",["t"]="The Crimson Threat"}}}}}
t["npc:executor-zygand"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,297,16.392.0,22.341.0,23.236.0,33.146.0,46.239.0,31.198.0,49.226.0,53.231.0",["h"]="c8df6d",["n"]="Ejecutor Zygand",["s"]="Ejecutor Zygand. El Ejecutor Zygand es un veterano comandante de los Renegados apostado en el ayuntamiento de Rémol, que supervisa las operaciones defensivas y militares por el centro de los Claros de Tirisfal. Rindiendo cuentas directamente al alto mando de Entrañas, coordina la purga de las fuerzas de la Cruzada Escarlata que se adentran en territorio Renegado. Situado en el corazón administrativo de Rémol, el Ejecutor Zygand coordina la defensa regional de los Renegados tras su despertar inicial en Camposanto. Como superior directo de oficiales regionales como el Ejecutor Arren y de centinelas de campo como la Guardia de la Muerte Linnea, Zygand recopila los informes de los exploradores y envía a reclutas cualificados a salvaguardar las fronteras de Lordaeron de posibles incursiones.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Travelers from Kalimdor visiting Tirisfal Glades see in Zygand the structured, disciplined military leadership driving the Forsaken's struggle to secure Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken venturing out of Deathknell, Executor Zygand represents the wider military authority of the Undercity, welcoming new citizens into active service against their bitterest enemies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken officer operating out of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He commands local Deathguard garrisons, receives tactical reports from lower-ranking officers, and directs military campaigns against local threats.",["al"]={"zygand","who is executor zygand","zygand role"},["q"]="Who is Executor Zygand?"},{["a"]="He is located inside or near the main town hall of Brill, the central Forsaken settlement in Tirisfal Glades situated just north of the Undercity.",["al"]={"zygand location","where is zygand","executor zygand map"},["q"]="Where can I find Executor Zygand?"},{["a"]="His primary focus is orchestrating the regional war against the Scarlet Crusade. He monitors the zealots' movements throughout Tirisfal and issues orders to dismantle their encampments and leadership before they can march on the Undercity.",["al"]={"zygand quest goal","why fight crusade","zygand purpose"},["q"]="What is Zygand's main goal in Tirisfal Glades?"},{["a"]="Zygand acts as the superior officer to Executor Arren, who directs initial recruits in Deathknell, as well as field sentries like Deathguard Linnea patrolling the main crossroads of Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"zygand subordinates","who serves zygand","arren superior"},["q"]="Who reports to Executor Zygand?"},{["a"]="Yes. In addition to fighting the Scarlet Crusade, Zygand issues regional bounties to eliminate feral undead and dangerous rogue scavengers, such as the corpse-stealing gnoll Maggot Eye, that endanger travel through the glades.",["al"]={"maggot eye","zygand bounties","wanted quests"},["q"]="Does Executor Zygand handle rogue undead threats?"},{["a"]="An Executor serves as a regional governor and military commander within the Forsaken hierarchy. They manage settlements, command local units of the Deathguard, and enforce Queen Sylvanas's rule across Lordaeron's contested regions.",["al"]={"what is an executor","executor rank","forsaken executor"},["q"]="What rank does an 'Executor' hold among the Forsaken?"}},["kw"]={"arren","brill","deathguard","executor","maggot eye","scarlet crusade","tirisfal","zygand"},["n"]="Executor Zygand",["s"]="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken commander stationed at the town hall in Brill, overseeing defensive and military operations across central Tirisfal Glades. Reporting directly to the Undercity's high command, he coordinates the purge of Scarlet Crusade forces pressing into Forsaken territory.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned at the administrative heart of Brill, Executor Zygand coordinates regional defense for the Forsaken after their initial awakening in Deathknell. Serving as the direct superior to regional officers like Executor Arren and field sentries such as Deathguard Linnea, Zygand synthesizes scout intelligence and dispatches able recruits to safeguard Lordaeron's borders from encroachment.",["t"]="Command in Brill"},{["b"]="Zygand's primary military concern is the fanatic presence of the Scarlet Crusade, which infests outposts across Tirisfal Glades. Under his direction, agents are sent systematically to strike at Crusader scouts, encampments, and forward bases, ensuring the zealots never muster sufficient strength to threaten the approaches to the Undercity.",["t"]="The War on the Crusade"}}}}}
t["npc:fandral-staghelm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,417,23.647.0,29.638.0,18.306.0,24.261.0,43.290.0,54.286.0,31.269.0,36.135.0",["h"]="5c70f9",["n"]="Fandral Corzocelada",["s"]="Fandral Corzocelada. El archidruida Fandral Corzocelada lidera a los druidas del Círculo Cenarion desde el Enclave Cenarion en Darnassus. Al asumir el poder tras la desaparición de Malfurión Tempestira en el Sueño Esmeralda, impulsó la plantación del nuevo Árbol del Mundo, Teldrassil. Orgulloso, arisco e implacablemente ambicioso, Fandral aboga por un resurgimiento agresivo de los kaldorei que a menudo lo enfrenta a la suma sacerdotisa Tyrande Susurravientos. Tras la Tercera Guerra y el sacrificio de Nordrassil en la cima del Monte Hyjal, los elfos de la noche perdieron su inmortalidad y su sagrado santuario. Mientras Malfurión Tempestira aconsejaba paciencia y advertía contra la vanidad, Fandral defendió la audaz creación de un nuevo Árbol del Mundo frente a la costa de Kalimdor. Cuando Malfurión cayó en coma posteriormente en el Sueño Esmeralda, Fandral tomó la iniciativa y guio a los druidas para erigir Teldrassil. Concibió la colosal rama como un monumento a la resistencia de los kaldorei y un medio para restaurar su supremacía perdida, aun cuando los Aspectos Dragón negaron deliberadamente sus bendiciones a tal empresa no consentida.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Staghelm commands the Darnassian druids, pushing the Cenarion Circle toward direct worldly authority while clashing with the traditional teachings of the sleeping Malfurion Stormrage.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though Teldrassil serves as an Alliance bastion in northern Kalimdor, Staghelm views the younger races with thinly veiled disdain, tolerating their presence only as political expediency demands.",["race:NightElf"]="As one of Darnassus's primary leaders, Fandral embodies Kaldorei pride and fury, driving the settlement of Teldrassil even as ordinary citizens feel the rift between his enclave and the Temple of the Moon."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fandral Staghelm is the acting Archdruid of the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus, presiding over Kaldorei druids in Malfurion Stormrage's absence. Known for his fiery temperament and imperial ambitions, he is the primary visionary behind the creation of Teldrassil.",["al"]={"fandral lore","who is the archdruid","archdruid of darnassus"},["q"]="Who is Fandral Staghelm?"},{["a"]="Fandral advocates for Kaldorei military resurgence, aggressive expansion, and reclaiming lost immortality. Tyrande Whisperwind pursues cautious spiritual guidance through Elune. Their competing visions for the night elves' post-Hyjal future spark fierce political friction within Darnassus.",["al"]={"fandral and tyrande","why do druids and priestesses disagree","staghelm vs whisperwind"},["q"]="Why doesn't Fandral get along with Tyrande?"},{["a"]="Malfurion believed planting a replacement for Nordrassil was an act of hubris that nature would not condone. When Malfurion vanished into his coma, Fandral rallied the remaining druids to plant Teldrassil regardless, seeking to restore Kaldorei power and reclaim their lost immortality.",["al"]={"who created teldrassil","why did fandral plant teldrassil","origin of teldrassil"},["q"]="Why was Teldrassil planted against Malfurion's wishes?"},{["a"]="During the War of the Shifting Sands in Silithus, Fandral's son Valstann was lured into an ambush at Southwind Village. The qiraji General Rajaxx captured Valstann and slaughtered him in front of Fandral, leaving the Archdruid grief-stricken and permanently embittered.",["al"]={"fandral son","who was valstann","valstann staghelm"},["q"]="What happened to Fandral's son?"},{["a"]="Fandral stands atop the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus, surrounded by his loyal druids and overseeable business of the Kaldorei capital.",["al"]={"where is fandral","fandral location","cenarion enclave leader"},["q"]="Where can Fandral Staghelm be found?"}},["kw"]={"cenarion circle","darnassus","fandral","malfurion","rajaxx","shifting sands","staghelm","teldrassil","valstann"},["n"]="Fandral Staghelm",["s"]="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids of the Cenarion Circle from the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus. Stepping into power after Malfurion Stormrage vanished into the Emerald Dream, he championed the planting of the new World Tree, Teldrassil. Proud, abrasive, and relentlessly ambitious, Fandral advocates for an aggressive Kaldorei resurgence that frequently pits him against High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the Third War and the sacrifice of Nordrassil atop Mount Hyjal, the night elves lost their immortality and their sacred sanctuary. While Malfurion Stormrage cautioned patience and warned against vanity, Fandral championed the bold creation of a new World Tree off the coast of Kalimdor. When Malfurion subsequently fell comatose within the Emerald Dream, Fandral seized the initiative and led the druids in raising Teldrassil. He envisioned the colossal bough as a monument to Kaldorei endurance and a vessel to restore their lost supremacy, even though the Dragon Aspects pointedly withheld their blessings from the unapproved endeavor.",["t"]="Architect of Teldrassil"},{["b"]="A millennium before the First War, Fandral served as the Kaldorei field commander in Silithus during the War of the Shifting Sands. Renowned among the insectoid qiraji as 'Kar'sis'—the Hand of Earth—he held the front lines alongside his beloved only son, Valstann. Exploiting Fandral's devotion, the qiraji General Rajaxx engineered a feint against Southwind Village and captured Valstann, ruthlessly executing him directly in front of the horrified Archdruid. The loss shattered Fandral's spirit, precipitating a devastating retreat and cementing an abiding, bitter hatred for the swarm that remains etched into his haughty demeanor.",["t"]="Tragedy in the Shifting Sands"},{["b"]="Within the marble boughs of Darnassus, Fandral governs Kaldorei affairs with a haughty, unyielding hand. Unlike High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, who favors spiritual preservation and cautious diplomacy, Fandral views military expansion and decisive strength as paramount to the survival of their people.",["t"]="Rivalry and Hubris"}}}}}
t["npc:farthing"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,272,21.374.0,24.390.0,35.119.0,46.199.0,39.187.0,60.172.0",["h"]="116e77",["n"]="Lontananza",["s"]="Lontananza. El Obispo Lontananza es un clérigo humano que reside en la Catedral de la Luz, en la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Ante visitantes y devotos, se presenta como un devoto siervo de la Sagrada Luz que guía a los feligreses y canaliza ayuda hacia los asentamientos asediados de todo el reino. Entre las serenas salas de mármol de la Catedral de la Luz, el Obispo Lontananza se erige como una de las figuras destacadas dedicadas a atender las necesidades espirituales de la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Junto al Arzobispo Benedictus y al resto del clero congregado, ofrece consejo a los viajeros, asiste a quienes se instruyen en las artes sagradas y se ocupa de las obligaciones cívicas y pastorales de la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="For priests visiting the Cathedral of Light, Farthing represents the established hierarchy and scholarly wisdom of the human clergy in Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="Adventurers battling the creeping corruption in southern Alliance territories such as Duskwood look to Farthing and his fellow clergy for divine insight and spiritual resolve."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bishop Farthing resides inside the Cathedral of Light, located at the center of Cathedral Square within Stormwind City.",["al"]={"farthing location","where is farthing","farthing map"},["q"]="Where can Bishop Farthing be found?"},{["a"]="He serves as an ordained bishop within the Church of the Holy Light, offering guidance to visiting faithful, priests in training, and adventurers seeking holy wisdom on behalf of distant settlements.",["al"]={"what does farthing do","who is farthing"},["q"]="What role does Farthing play in the Cathedral?"},{["a"]="Farthing is sought out by adventurers dealing with the undead menace in Duskwood, advising on the dark arts sustaining the necromancer Morbent Fel and directing souls toward purification.",["al"]={"farthing duskwood","farthing morbent fel"},["q"]="How is Farthing involved with Duskwood?"},{["a"]="Several other individuals across human lands share the surname Farthing, including Coleman and Yvette Farthing, though he does not actively speak of any direct family ties.",["al"]={"coleman farthing relative","farthing family"},["q"]="Is Farthing related to other citizens bearing the same name?"}},["kw"]={"benedictus","bishop farthing","cathedral of light","farthing","morbent fel","seeking wisdom","stormwind"},["n"]="Farthing",["s"]="Bishop Farthing is a human clergyman residing within the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. To visitors and worshippers, he presents himself as a devout servant of the Holy Light who guides parishioners and directs aid toward beleaguered settlements across the kingdom.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the serene marble halls of the Cathedral of Light, Bishop Farthing stands as one of the prominent figures attending to the spiritual needs of Stormwind City. Alongside Archbishop Benedictus and the gathered clergy, he offers counsel to travelers, assists those pursuing the holy arts, and attends to the civic and pastoral obligations of the Church of the Holy Light.",["t"]="A Bishop in Stormwind"},{["b"]="Despite remaining situated within the capital, Farthing directs earnest travelers toward darker corners of the kingdom that desperately require holy aid. When troubled reports filter in regarding the necromancer Morbent Fel and the creeping undead blight overtaking Duskwood, Farthing serves as an advisor in seeking out methods to overcome dark sorceries and cleanse the blighted frontier.",["t"]="Aid to the Plagued Lands"}}}}}
t["npc:fenrus-the-devourer"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,322,29.436.0,15.369.0,21.397.1,32.260.0,26.167.0,33.157.0,54.234.0,47.174.0,55.191.0",["h"]="3bfe10",["n"]="Fenrus el Devorador",["s"]="Fenrus el Devorador. Fenrus el Devorador es un enorme huargo que merodea por el sagrario superior del Castillo de Colmillo Oscuro. Mantenido como mascota personal y guardián por el Archimago Arugal, la voraz bestia está hinchada de magias antinaturales. Cualquiera que se atreva a traspasar el estudio personal del archimago debe enfrentarse a este horror salvaje y al amo que vela por él. En lo profundo del Castillo de Colmillo Oscuro, a las puertas de los aposentos personales del Archimago Arugal, acecha el monstruoso huargo conocido como Fenrus el Devorador. A diferencia de los huargen lupinos que recorren las almenas, Fenrus es un verdadero huargo, hinchado hasta alcanzar proporciones gigantescas. Merodeando entre estanterías, pergaminos y aparatos arcanos del estudio privado de Arugal, la bestia sirve tanto de mascota como de violento guardia perimetral contra cualquier intruso que busque la cabeza del mago loco.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Do not waste time attempting to charm Fenrus. The beast's mind is irrevocably twisted by Shadowfang's dark arts and cannot be bound by the wild.",["class:Mage"]="Fenrus stands as a grim reminder of how far Archmage Arugal has fallen, using arcane arts to warp wild beasts into grotesque domestic guardians.",["class:Warlock"]="Archmage Arugal's ability to summon voidwalkers to aid his hound reveals how deeply the former Dalaran mage has delved into shadowy, forbidden conjurations."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Fenrus is an exceptionally large worg, a natural wolf-like predator indigenous to Lordaeron, rather than a bipedal worgen. His unnatural bulk and vicious ferocity are the direct results of prolonged exposure to the dark magic practicing within Shadowfang Keep.",["al"]={"is fenrus a worgen","fenrus creature type","fenrus wolf"},["q"]="What kind of creature is Fenrus?"},{["a"]="Fenrus prowls the study chambers high inside Shadowfang Keep in Silverpine Forest. His lair is situated directly along the approach to Archmage Arugal's inner redoubt.",["al"]={"where is fenrus","fenrus location","fenrus room"},["q"]="Where can Fenrus be found?"},{["a"]="No. Despite being an ordinary beast by classification, Fenrus cannot be tamed. His mind is thoroughly broken, feral, and tied to Archmage Arugal's dark will.",["al"]={"can i tame fenrus","is fenrus tameable","taming fenrus"},["q"]="Can hunters tame Fenrus as a pet?"},{["a"]="Arugal views Fenrus as his prized pet and final line of defense before his sanctum. When Fenrus bellows upon entering combat, Arugal intervenes directly, conjuring voidwalkers into the chamber to overwhelm whoever threatens his beast.",["al"]={"arugal voidwalkers","why does arugal help fenrus","fenrus voidwalker add"},["q"]="Why does Arugal summon demons when Fenrus is attacked?"},{["a"]="Fenrus's massive size is believed to be the consequence of Archmage Arugal's dark magical experimentation, or magical fallout from the worgen infestation overtaking the keep.",["al"]={"why is fenrus huge","fenrus size lore","giant worg"},["q"]="Why is Fenrus so much larger than normal worgs?"},{["a"]="When Fenrus engages in combat, he unleashes a thunderous roar so loud it can be heard by anyone anywhere inside Shadowfang Keep, alerting all to the battle taking place outside Arugal's door.",["al"]={"fenrus roar","fenrus howl across dungeon","loud roar sfk"},["q"]="What happens across the dungeon when Fenrus is engaged?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","fenrus","fenrus the devourer","shadowfang keep","silverpine","worg"},["n"]="Fenrus the Devourer",["s"]="Fenrus the Devourer is an enormous worg that prowls the upper sanctum of Shadowfang Keep. Kept as a personal pet and guardian by Archmage Arugal, the ravenous beast is bloated on unnatural magics. Anyone daring to breach the archmage's personal study must contend with this feral horror and the master who watches over it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Deep within Shadowfang Keep, just outside Archmage Arugal's personal chambers, lurks the monstrous worg known as Fenrus the Devourer. Unlike the lupine worgen roaming the ramparts, Fenrus is an actual worg, swollen to gargantuan proportions. Prowling the shelves, scrolls, and arcane apparatuses of Arugal's private study, the beast serves both as a pet and as a violent perimeter guard against any intruder seeking the mad mage's head.",["t"]="A Beast in the Master's Study"},{["b"]="Fenrus's unnatural bulk suggests he was subjected to the dark magics saturating the keep since Baron Silverlaine's downfall. Archmage Arugal or his unleashed worgen clearly warped the creature with arcane or shadowy experiments, transforming a native predator into a ravenous juggernaut. Fenrus is so feral and magically bound that no hunter can charm or tame his mind.",["t"]="Corrupted Might"},{["b"]="Disturbing Fenrus is an immediate death sentence for the careless. When the beast spots an intruder, it lets loose an ear-splitting howl that echoes across the entire fortress, drawing the direct attention of Arugal himself. Rather than leaving his pet undefended, the archmage projects his dark will into the chamber, summoning voidwalkers to assist Fenrus in overwhelming and devouring invaders.",["t"]="Arugal's Watchful Eye"}}}}}
t["npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,397,15.367.0,27.366.0,19.390.1,30.232.0,26.212.0,32.182.0,51.206.0,26.197.0,34.173.0",["h"]="3c5fb7",["n"]="Primer oficial Fistimos",["s"]="Primer oficial Fistimos. El Primer oficial Fistimos es un marinero andrajoso y maloliente que pasa los días bebiendo frente al Mesón Aguahonda, en el Puerto de Menethil. Antaño primer oficial a bordo del Wave Mistress de La Tercera Flota de Kul Tiras, es el único superviviente conocido con vida de la destrucción de la flota durante la Segunda Guerra. Atormentado por la tragedia, busca aventureros dispuestos a enfrentarse a los espíritus inquietos de sus camaradas ahogados. Tumbado frente al Mesón Aguahonda en medio del húmedo aire salino del Puerto de Menethil, el Primer oficial Fistimos es un hombre fácil de pasar por alto, o de evitar por completo debido a su hedor a falta de aseo. Para la mayoría de los parroquianos, no es más que otro viejo lobo de mar acabado que ahoga sus recuerdos en alcohol. Sin embargo, quienes estén dispuestos a sentarse y escuchar oirán relatos desgarradores sobre una orgullosa flota abatida por el fuego y las garras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Fitzsimmons represents a tragic chapter in Alliance naval history, reminding heroes of the catastrophic losses suffered against the Horde's enslaved dragon armada.",["race:Human"]="As a veteran of Kul Tiras, Fitzsimmons shares deep cultural ties with the seafaring human kingdom that sacrificed much to defend Lordaeron during the Second War."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is an old Kul Tiran sailor and former first mate of the Wave Mistress. He survived the catastrophic sinking of Kul Tiras's Third Fleet during the Second War and now drinks his days away outside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern.",["al"]={"fitzsimmons lore","who is fitzsimmons","first mate fitzsimmons"},["q"]="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?"},{["a"]="The Wave Mistress and the rest of the Third Fleet were ambushed by enslaved red dragons ridden by the Dragonmaw clan during the Second War. The vessels were burned and broken upon the reef off the Wetlands coast.",["al"]={"what happened to wave mistress","third fleet destruction","why did his ship sink"},["q"]="What happened to his ship?"},{["a"]="The shattered hulls of the fleet lie submerged along the rocky coastline north of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, now guarded by murlocs and the restless spirits of drowned sailors.",["al"]={"lost fleet location","where are the sunken ships","fitzsimmons ship location"},["q"]="Where is the Lost Fleet located?"},{["a"]="The drowned sailors of the Third Fleet rose as cursed, tormented undead rather than passing on. Fitzsimmons seeks brave travelers to put them to rest and retrieve the artifacts keeping their souls shackled.",["al"]={"cursed crew quest lore","why kill his crew"},["q"]="Why does he want adventurers to fight his old crew?"},{["a"]="It is an ancient, potent artifact carried aboard the Third Fleet. Its dark power is tied to the curse afflicting the sunken sailors, making its recovery crucial to granting the drowned fleet peace.",["al"]={"eye of paleth","paleth relic"},["q"]="What is the Eye of Paleth?"},{["a"]="Having lost everything when his fleet went down, Fitzsimmons has lived in drunken neglect outside the Deepwater Tavern for years, wearing sea-soaked rags and rarely washing.",["al"]={"why does fitzsimmons smell","fitzsimmons stench"},["q"]="Why does Fitzsimmons smell so bad?"}},["kw"]={"deepwater tavern","eye of paleth","first mate fitzsimmons","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","lost fleet","menethil harbor","third fleet","wave mistress"},["n"]="First Mate Fitzsimmons",["s"]="First Mate Fitzsimmons is a ragged, reeking sailor who spends his days drinking outside the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Once the first mate aboard the Wave Mistress of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet, he is the sole known living survivor of the fleet's destruction during the Second War. Haunted by the tragedy, he seeks willing adventurers to face the restless spirits of his drowned comrades.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Lounging outside the Deepwater Tavern amid the damp salt air of Menethil Harbor, First Mate Fitzsimmons is an easy man to overlook—or avoid entirely, given his unwashed stench. To most patrons, he is just another broken old salt drinking his memories away. Yet those willing to sit and listen will hear harrowing tales of a proud fleet brought low by fire and claw.",["t"]="A Broken Sailor"},{["b"]="During the Second War, Fitzsimmons served as first mate aboard the Wave Mistress, part of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet dispatched to fight the Horde. Off the coast of the Wetlands, the fleet was ambushed and incinerated by enslaved red dragons flown by Dragonmaw orcs. The ships were shattered and sunk, leaving Fitzsimmons as the only man to drag himself ashore alive.",["t"]="The Fall of the Third Fleet"},{["b"]="Surviving the dragonfire did not bring Fitzsimmons peace. The remains of the ships, now remembered as the Lost Fleet, are haunted by his former crewmates, who rose as cursed undead unable to rest in their watery graves. Driven by guilt and terror, Fitzsimmons recruits travelers to put down the undead sailors and recover ancient relics that might finally lift the evil binding their souls.",["t"]="The Lingering Curse"}}}}}
t["npc:foreman-oslow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,413,17.430.0,29.449.0,21.172.0,35.246.0,29.155.0,40.213.0,48.158.0,35.193.0",["h"]="e8560f",["n"]="Supervisor Olento",["s"]="Supervisor Olento. El Supervisor Olento es el asediado maestro de obras de Villa del Lago, encargado de reparar el derruido puente del Lago Sempiterno en el corazón de las Montañas Crestagrana. Acosado por la artillería de los orcos Rocanegra y los asaltantes grolls, sus esfuerzos de reconstrucción se han estancado debido a envíos perdidos y equipo hundido. Depende en gran medida de los aventureros errantes para recuperar su equipo y asegurar materiales para que Villa del Lago pueda reconectar su ruta comercial vital. Junto a la mampostería fracturada del puente del Lago Sempiterno, el Supervisor Olento se enfrenta a una ardua batalla. El puente es la arteria de Villa del Lago, cruzando la extensión del Lago Sempiterno y uniendo los caminos occidentales hacia Elwynn con las costas orientales. Los orcos Rocanegra, descendiendo de los riscos de Petravista, atacaron el paso para inutilizar la logística y el movimiento militar de la villa, dejándola dividida y vulnerable.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire's severed bridge leaves the eastern frontier exposed, making Oslow's restoration efforts a strategic necessity for securing the Alliance border.",["profession:Mining"]="Oslow relies on raw materials, metalwork, and quarry shipments to rebuild broken masonry, keeping him intimately tied to local mineral deliveries."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Foreman Oslow is a human stonemason and builder stationed in Lakeshire. He is the head craftsman responsible for the maintenance and reconstruction of the Everstill Bridge.",["al"]={"foreman oslow","who is oslow","lakeshire builder"},["q"]="Who is Foreman Oslow?"},{["a"]="The Everstill Bridge was shattered by the Blackrock orcs of Redridge Mountains. Destroying the span severed Lakeshire's main thoroughfare, severely weakening the town's defenses and cutting off easy transit between the eastern and western shores.",["al"]={"why is the bridge broken","who broke lakeshire bridge","everstill bridge destroyed"},["q"]="Why is the Everstill Bridge broken?"},{["a"]="Oslow's heavy toolbox rests at the bottom of Lake Everstill. The boat transporting them from Goldshire was struck and sunk by a Blackrock catapult barrage.",["al"]={"where are the tools","lost tools location","oslow toolbox"},["q"]="Where are Oslow's lost tools?"},{["a"]="Between orc catapult fire sinking his tools in the lake and gnolls stealing building supplies from incoming shipments, Oslow lacks the necessary materials and equipment to resume construction without outside help.",["al"]={"why is bridge not fixed","lakeshire bridge delay"},["q"]="Why hasn't the bridge been repaired yet?"},{["a"]="His replacement tools were originally carted in on a wagon from Goldshire in Elwynn Forest before being transferred to a lake ferry to bypass the broken span.",["al"]={"supply wagon origin","where did tools come from"},["q"]="Where did Oslow's supplies come from originally?"},{["a"]="Oslow faces constant harassment from two fronts: the Blackrock clan orcs entrenched in the nearby heights, whose siege engines bombard the lake, and prowling gnolls who pick off supply convoys.",["al"]={"oslow enemies","who attacks the bridge"},["q"]="What threats is Oslow dealing with?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock","everstill bridge","foreman oslow","goldshire","lakeshire","oslow","redridge","toolbox"},["n"]="Foreman Oslow",["s"]="Foreman Oslow is Lakeshire's beleaguered master builder, tasked with repairing the ruined Everstill Bridge in the heart of Redridge Mountains. Beset by Blackrock orc artillery and gnoll raiders, his reconstruction efforts have stalled due to lost shipments and sunken equipment. He relies heavily on traveling adventurers to retrieve his gear and secure materials so Lakeshire can reconnect its vital trade route.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing by the fractured masonry of the Everstill Bridge, Foreman Oslow faces an uphill battle. The bridge is the lifeline of Lakeshire, spanning the expanse of Lake Everstill and linking the western roads toward Elwynn to the eastern shores. Blackrock orcs, sweeping down from the crags of Stonewatch, targeted the crossing to cripple the town's logistics and military movement, leaving the settlement splintered and vulnerable.",["t"]="A Town Cut in Two"},{["b"]="Every attempt Oslow makes to rebuild seems plagued by misfortune. When the bridge fell, his replacement tools were shipped overland from Goldshire and loaded onto a lake ferry. Orc catapult crews caught the vessel in their sights, sending his heavy iron toolbox straight to the muddy bed of Lake Everstill. To compound matters, local Redridge gnolls ambushed his supply wagons, making off with timber and mortar rivets necessary to raise the arches.",["t"]="Sunken Steel and Stolen Stone"}}}}}
t["npc:furen-longbeard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,369,36.416.0,29.380.0,23.205.0,35.145.0,36.130.0,40.180.0,47.179.0,41.169.0",["h"]="32d24d",["n"]="Furen Barbalarga",["s"]="Furen Barbalarga. Furen Barbalarga es un maestro armero enano establecido en el bullicioso Distrito de los Enanos de la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Como aprendiz del renombrado herrero Grimand Elmore, se especializa en fabricar equipo de protección pesado y mallas resistentes para los avezados defensores de la Alianza. Guerreros de todo el reino acuden a él en busca de sus conocimientos de metalurgia para forjar armaduras especializadas y listas para el combate. Furen Barbalarga ejerce su oficio lejos de las grandes forjas de Forjaz, habiendo establecido su hogar entre los adoquines y el hollín del Distrito de los Enanos de Ventormenta. Como muchos de sus congéneres, Furen llevó la metalurgia tradicional enana hacia el sur para apoyar la reconstrucción y la defensa del reino. Trabajando entre fogones ardientes y yunques resonantes, mantiene estrechos lazos con otros artesanos por toda la ciudad y más allá.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="For Alliance warriors coming of age, Furen Longbeard is a pivotal contact who turns raw martial resolve and gathered reagents into vital, fire-hardened defensive armor.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Furen represents the high standards of dwarven smithing established in Stormwind, showcasing advanced techniques passed down by Grimand Elmore.",["race:Dwarf"]="Even far from Ironforge, Furen Longbeard keeps dwarven metallurgical traditions alive in the heart of the human capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Furen Longbeard is a dwarven armorer operating out of the Dwarven District in Stormwind City. He serves as an essential contact and mentor for Alliance warriors looking to acquire mastercrafted mail armor.",["al"]={"who is furen","furen longbeard lore","dwarf armorer stormwind"},["q"]="Who is Furen Longbeard?"},{["a"]="He is located in the Dwarven District of Stormwind City, standing near the bustling forges and smithing workshops that dominate the neighborhood.",["al"]={"where is furen longbeard","furen longbeard location","furen stormwind"},["q"]="Where can Furen Longbeard be found?"},{["a"]="Furen was taught armorcraft and metallurgy by Grimand Elmore, a respected veteran craftsman also residing in the Dwarven District.",["al"]={"furen teacher","furen mentor","who trained furen"},["q"]="Who taught Furen his smithing craft?"},{["a"]="He is renowned for fashioning Fire Hardened Mail, a resilient set of armor created through exacting metallurgical processes requiring rare components gathered across the continent.",["al"]={"fire hardened mail","furen armor quest","warrior mail quest stormwind"},["q"]="What armor is Furen famous for crafting?"},{["a"]="He shares his clan name with several other prominent dwarves across the Eastern Kingdoms, such as the seasoned mountaineer Pilot Longbeard, though he focuses strictly on smithing.",["al"]={"furen family","longbeard clan","pilot longbeard relative"},["q"]="Is Furen Longbeard related to other Longbeards?"},{["a"]="Warriors who have proven their basic martial prowess are directed to Furen to obtain heavy, durable armor capable of enduring front-line combat against deadlier threats.",["al"]={"why do warriors visit furen","warrior quest dwarven district","furen warrior trainer"},["q"]="Why do warriors seek out Furen Longbeard?"}},["kw"]={"armorer","blacksmith","dwarven district","fire hardened mail","furen longbeard","grimand elmore","stormwind","warrior"},["n"]="Furen Longbeard",["s"]="Furen Longbeard is a master dwarven armorer stationed within Stormwind City's bustling Dwarven District. Apprenticed under the renowned smith Grimand Elmore, he specializes in crafting heavy protective gear and sturdy mail for seasoned defenders of the Alliance. Warriors across the kingdom seek out his metallurgical expertise to forge specialized, battle-ready armor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Furen Longbeard plies his craft far from the great forges of Ironforge, making his home instead among the cobblestones and soot of Stormwind's Dwarven District. Like many of his kin, Furen brought traditional dwarven metallurgy south to support the rebuilding and defense of the kingdom. Working amidst blazing hearths and clanging anvils, he maintains strong ties with other artisans throughout the city and beyond.",["t"]="A Dwarven Smith in the Human Capital"},{["b"]="Taught by the venerable craftsman Grimand Elmore, Furen has perfected techniques for treating heavy mail and plate to withstand extreme battlefield punishment. Promising young warriors seeking durable protection often turn to Furen, who requires rare ores, specialized components, and exotic reagents from distant corners of the world to fashion his signature fire-hardened armor.",["t"]="Mastery of Fire-Hardened Mail"}}}}}
t["npc:gakin-the-darkbinder"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,297,24.429.0,16.411.0,24.365.1,38.247.0,34.223.0,52.230.0,22.201.0,36.153.0,46.232.0",["h"]="8f5b5b",["n"]="Gakin el Presotenebra",["s"]="Gakin el Presotenebra. Gakin el Presotenebra es un maestro brujo que opera en secreto en las profundidades de la taberna El Cordero Degollado, en el Barrio de los Magos de Ventormenta. Instruye a los aspirantes de la Alianza en las artes oscuras y pone a prueba su determinación antes de iniciar rituales para invocar y someter a demonios de otros mundos a su servicio. Mientras los magos de Ventormenta practican abiertamente en sus imponentes santuarios, los practicantes de las sombras y lo vil deben morar donde las miradas indiscretas no puedan llegar. Oculto bajo la sala común de El Cordero Degollado hay un sótano húmedo similar a una cripta, equipado con círculos de invocación y siniestros tomos. Gakin ejerce como eje central de este cónclave oculto, asegurándose de que los jóvenes brujos aprendan disciplina y moderación antes de desatar horrores que no puedan controlar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="Gakin is a vital mentor for human and gnome warlocks, offering pivotal class quests to master the voidwalker and succubus rituals in the crypts of Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="Operating secretly under the capital city, Gakin's coven demonstrates the pragmatic, shadow-drenched compromises made in the heart of the Alliance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gakin is located deep beneath The Slaughtered Lamb tavern in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind. Head inside the tavern, find the downward ramp at the back, and descend through the stone tunnels until you reach the summoning circle in the lowest crypt.",["al"]={"where is gakin","gakin location","slaughtered lamb basement"},["q"]="Where can I find Gakin the Darkbinder?"},{["a"]="He serves as a prominent warlock quest-giver and mentor for Alliance characters. He tests novitiates by sending them on trials across Azeroth and teaching them how to summon and bind demons like the Voidwalker and Succubus.",["al"]={"what does gakin do","gakin role","gakin quests"},["q"]="What does Gakin the Darkbinder do?"},{["a"]="Demonic magic is forbidden and deeply mistrusted in Stormwind. The practitioners under The Slaughtered Lamb operate in strict secrecy, tolerated only as a dangerous covert asset and hidden away from the city's guards and citizens.",["al"]={"why are warlocks allowed","are warlocks legal in stormwind","slaughtered lamb lore"},["q"]="Why are warlocks allowed under The Slaughtered Lamb?"},{["a"]="Surena Caledon was a former student of Gakin who stole a powerful Bloodstone Choker from him. Her betrayal poses a danger to their hidden order, prompting Gakin to task warlocks with tracking her down.",["al"]={"surena caledon","gakin student","who stole from gakin"},["q"]="Who is Surena Caledon?"},{["a"]="Gakin oversees the binding rituals for both Voidwalkers and Succubi, guiding warlocks to draw the creatures into the subterranean circle and subdue them.",["al"]={"gakin demons","gakin voidwalker","gakin succubus"},["q"]="Which demons does Gakin help summon?"},{["a"]="Strahad Farsan is an experienced warlock residing in the Ratchet hills of Kalimdor. Once a student advances past Gakin's fundamental binding rituals, Gakin directs them across the sea to continue their darker education with Strahad.",["al"]={"strahad","seeking strahad","where does gakin send me next"},["q"]="Who is Strahad and why does Gakin mention him?"}},["kw"]={"darkbinder","gakin","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","succubus","surena caledon","voidwalker","warlock"},["n"]="Gakin the Darkbinder",["s"]="Gakin the Darkbinder is a master warlock operating covertly deep beneath The Slaughtered Lamb tavern in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. He instructs aspiring Alliance practitioners in the dark arts, testing their resolve before initiating rituals to summon and bind otherworldly demons to their service.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Stormwind's mages practice openly in their towering sanctuaries, practitioners of shadow and fel must dwell where prying eyes cannot reach. Hidden below the taproom of The Slaughtered Lamb is a damp crypt-like cellar equipped with summoning circles and grim tomes. Gakin serves as the anchor of this hidden conclave, ensuring that young warlocks learn discipline and restraint before unleashing horrors they cannot control.",["t"]="A Secret Gathering Place"},{["b"]="Gakin's expertise lies in demonology and binding rituals. Initiates who earn his notice are sent across the kingdom to acquire rare relics and ingredients—from stolen bloodstone talismans to corrupt wood from the dark forests. Once the reagents are assembled, Gakin oversees rituals in the crypt's summoning circle, forcing novitiates to subjugate voidwalkers and succubi in life-or-death trials of willpower.",["t"]="Master of Demons"},{["b"]="Not all of Gakin's students remain obedient. One former apprentice, Surena Caledon, absconded with a valuable Bloodstone Choker, fleeing into the wilds. Such internal treacheries threaten to expose the warlock circle to the city guards, prompting Gakin to dispatch loyal followers to recover lost artifacts and silence loose ends before the authorities take notice.",["t"]="Betrayals and Loose Ends"}}}}}
t["npc:gan-rul-bloodeye"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,344,23.407.0,18.364.0,24.187.0,34.188.0,47.285.0,37.219.0,35.100.0,38.198.0",["h"]="c7d608",["n"]="Ojo sangriento de Gan'rul",["s"]="Ojo sangriento de Gan'rul. Ojo sangriento de Gan'rul es un veterano instructor de brujos orco que reside en las profundidades de la oscura caverna del Circo de las Sombras, en Orgrimmar. Oculto a la atenta mirada de la ciudad de la superficie, inicia a los brujos de la Horda en ritos demoníacos más oscuros. Bajo su tutela, los iniciados aprenden a someter a su voluntad a entidades de otros mundos, como abisarios y súcubos. Aunque el Jefe de Guerra Thrall tolera la presencia de brujos en la nueva Horda, sus artes oscuras no son bienvenidas a plena luz del sol en Durotar. Ojo sangriento de Gan'rul tiene su morada en el Circo de las Sombras, un refugio subterráneo bajo Orgrimmar donde tejedores de sombras, pícaros y taumaturgos viles pueden estudiar sin ser molestados. Desde este enclave subterráneo, Gan'rul ejerce de tutor principal para los practicantes prometedores de la magia vil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="For warlocks seeking forbidden knowledge, Gan'rul is a vital mentor in Kalimdor, providing the knowledge and trials needed to bind voidwalkers and succubi.",["faction:Horde"]="Gan'rul embodies the precarious position of fel magic in Thrall's Horde—utilized for military strength, but confined to the underground recesses of the capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gan'rul Bloodeye is an orc warlock trainer stationed in Orgrimmar. He mentors novice and intermediate Horde warlocks, teaching them how to summon and bind demons from the Twisting Nether.",["al"]={"gan'rul bloodeye","who is ganrul","ganrul bloodeye role"},["q"]="Who is Gan'rul Bloodeye?"},{["a"]="He is located in the Cleft of Shadow, the subterranean cavern network hidden beneath Orgrimmar. He stands alongside fellow dark practitioners, away from the main thoroughfares of the city.",["al"]={"ganrul location","where is gan'rul bloodeye","where is cleft of shadow trainer"},["q"]="Where can I find Gan'rul Bloodeye?"},{["a"]="Warchief Thrall and the shamanistic society of the new Horde strongly distrust fel magic and demonic corruption after the orcs' past enslavement. Warlocks are permitted within the Horde strictly for their utility, but their practice is relegated to the shadows to prevent civic unrest.",["al"]={"why in caves","why hide warlocks","cleft of shadow lore"},["q"]="Why are warlocks hidden in the Cleft of Shadow?"},{["a"]="Gan'rul guides warlocks through the rituals required to summon and subjugate both the voidwalker and the succubus. Completing his tasks proves that the summoner possesses the necessary willpower to control these fiends.",["al"]={"demons ganrul teaches","ganrul demon quests","voidwalker succubus trainer"},["q"]="What demons does Gan'rul help summon?"},{["a"]="He shares a surname with Halga Bloodeye, though their precise relationship is not openly documented.",["al"]={"gan'rul relatives","halga bloodeye relative"},["q"]="Does Gan'rul have any known family?"},{["a"]="Strahad Farsan is an accomplished warlock residing in the Barrens near the Ratchet hills. Gan'rul eventually sends promising students to Strahad for more advanced instruction and greater challenges.",["al"]={"seeking strahad","who is strahad","strahad quest"},["q"]="Who is Strahad, whom Gan'rul mentions?"}},["kw"]={"bloodeye","cleft of shadow","gan'rul","orgrimmar","succubus","trainer","voidwalker","warlock"},["n"]="Gan'rul Bloodeye",["s"]="Gan'rul Bloodeye is a senior orc warlock trainer residing deep within the dark cavern of the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar. Hidden away from the watchful gaze of the city above, he initiates Horde warlocks into darker demonic rites. Under his instruction, initiates learn to bend otherworldly entities like voidwalkers and succubi to their will.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Warchief Thrall tolerates the presence of warlocks in the new Horde, their dark arts are not welcomed in the open sunlight of Durotar. Gan'rul Bloodeye makes his home in the Cleft of Shadow, a subterranean refuge beneath Orgrimmar where shadow weavers, rogues, and fel casters can study unmolested. From this subterranean perch, Gan'rul serves as a primary tutor for rising practitioners of fel magic.",["t"]="A Master in the Shadows"},{["b"]="Gan'rul's primary duty is overseeing the dangerous summoning rituals required of ambitious warlocks. Practitioners seeking to bind greater demons—such as the resilient voidwalker or the seductive succubus—must consult Gan'rul to secure ritual components and learn the precise incantations needed to dominate the summoned creature before it consumes its master.",["t"]="Binding the Nether"}}}}}
t["npc:gann-stonespire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,239,25.485.0,24.466.1,23.308.0,47.289.0,43.297.1,41.134.0",["h"]="6e32b1",["n"]="Gann Picopiedra",["s"]="Gann Picopiedra. Gann Picopiedra es un agraviado nómada tauren al que se encuentra vagando por los caminos del sur de Los Baldíos, cerca de Bael Modan. Expulsado de los cotos de caza ancestrales de su tribu por excavadores enanos, busca represalias contra el yacimiento arqueológico que no deja de expandirse. Antes de que la expedición enana llegara desde Forjaz para excavar la fortaleza de Bael Modan, las tierras circundantes servían como territorio ancestral y cotos de caza para la tribu de Gann Picopiedra. Los mineros enanos expulsaron a los tauren autóctonos de su suelo con picos, armas de fuego y maquinaria pesada, rechazando cualquier intento pacífico. Ahora, acampado junto al polvoriento camino del sur de Los Baldíos, Gann se niega a entregar su herencia en silencio y reúne a viajeros para contraatacar a los excavadores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Assisting Gann provides the Horde a vital tactical opportunity to blunt Alliance expansionism entrenched within the southern Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="Gann's plight represents the broader struggle of the nomadic tauren, whose ancestral ranges and sacred earth are repeatedly desecrated by foreign Alliance expeditions."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gann Stonespire is a tauren warrior whose tribe once inhabited the lands now occupied by the dwarven fortress of Bael Modan. Having been displaced when the dwarves established their dig site, he now waits by the roadside in the southern Barrens seeking vengeance and the reclamation of his people's homeland.",["al"]={"who is gann","gann stonespire lore","tauren outside bael modan"},["q"]="Who is Gann Stonespire?"},{["a"]="The Bael'dun dwarven expedition arrived in the southern Barrens and forcefully ejected the local tauren from their ancestral hunting grounds to construct their excavation fortress. After the dwarves rejected all diplomatic efforts, Gann resolved to dismantle their operation through force.",["al"]={"why does gann hate dwarves","why attack bael modan","gann bael modan conflict"},["q"]="Why is Gann fighting the dwarves of Bael Modan?"},{["a"]="Gann first commissions the death of dwarven overseers, including Prospector Khazgorm, to seize excavation records. Using stolen dwarven ordnance and blasting supplies, he then orchestrates the assembly of a bomb to destroy the expedition's flying machine and disrupt their technological dominance.",["al"]={"gann's revenge plan","what does gann do","bael modan bomb"},["q"]="What is Gann's plan against the excavation?"},{["a"]="He can be found wandering the road just west of Bael Modan in the southern Barrens, just outside the perimeter of the excavation site.",["al"]={"where is gann","gann stonespire location"},["q"]="Where does Gann Stonespire make his camp?"}},["kw"]={"bael modan","bael'dun","gann stonespire","prospector khazgorm","southern barrens","stonespire"},["n"]="Gann Stonespire",["s"]="Gann Stonespire is an aggrieved tauren nomad found wandering the roads of the southern Barrens near Bael Modan. Driven from his tribe's ancestral hunting grounds by dwarven excavators, he seeks retaliation against the encroaching dig site.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the dwarven expedition arrived from Ironforge to carve out the fortress of Bael Modan, the surrounding land served as ancestral territory and hunting grounds for Gann Stonespire's tribe. The dwarven miners drove the indigenous tauren from their soil with pickaxes, firearms, and heavy machinery, refusing peaceful overtures. Now camping along the dusty southern Barrens road, Gann refuses to quietly surrender his heritage, marshaling travelers to strike back at the excavators.",["t"]="Displaced from Bael Modan"},{["b"]="Recognizing that peaceful diplomacy has completely failed, Gann directs Horde operatives to break the dwarves' hold over the dig site. His retribution targets key expedition leadership, notably Prospector Khazgorm, before repurposing dwarven blasting powder and ordnance into an explosive charge. By detonating the contraption directly beneath the dwarven flying machine, Gann aims to cripple their technological advantage and reclaim honor for his displaced people.",["t"]="Reclamation and Sabotage"}}}}}
t["npc:gaxim-rustfizzle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,465,21.595.0,19.523.0,24.238.0,81.204.0,42.216.0,40.225.0,43.126.0,36.158.0",["h"]="afaaab",["n"]="Gaxim Silvóxido",["s"]="Gaxim Silvóxido. Gaxim Silvóxido es un ambicioso erudito y manitas gnomo destinado en un pequeño campamento de la Alianza a lo largo de la Senda de las Tejedoras en Sierra Espolón. Como representante de la Asamblea Iluminada de Arcanología, Alquimia e Ingeniería, busca demostrar a los escépticos elfos de la noche que los artificios avanzados y la alquimia pueden preservar su reino boscoso. Su curiosidad científica va acompañada de un profundo afán de venganza contra las destructivas operaciones de Ventura y Cía. Mientras que los elfos de la noche confían tradicionalmente en el druidismo ancestral y la magia de la naturaleza, Gaxim Silvóxido llegó a los escarpados desfiladeros de Sierra Espolón para demostrar una perspectiva radicalmente diferente. Como representante de la Asamblea Iluminada de Arcanología, Alquimia e Ingeniería, cree firmemente que los mecanismos calculados y las soluciones químicas pueden defender y restaurar las tierras vírgenes de Kalimdor con la misma eficacia que las plegarias a Elune. Acampado junto a la centinela Kaela Lanzasombra en la Senda de las Tejedoras, trabaja sin descanso para convencer a sus altos y solitarios aliados del valor ecológico de la ingeniería.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Perched on the perilous Webwinder Path, Gaxim provides crucial scouting, intelligence, and sabotage missions to check aggressive industrial incursions in Stonetalon.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gaxim puts engineering principles to work in the field, designing covert operations and tactical devices specifically tuned to disrupt crude Venture Company machinery.",["race:Gnome"]="Gaxim represents gnomish academic pride at its finest, showing Kalimdor's ancient cultures that gears and reagents can save a forest just as well as nature magic.",["race:NightElf"]="Though traditionalists may scoff at his whirring gadgets and bubbling vials, Gaxim is a steadfast ally actively defending Ashenvale and Stonetalon borders from goblin industry."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome scholar and inventor stationed at an Alliance lookout along the Webwinder Path in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an emissary for the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences.",["al"]={"who is gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle lore","gnome in stonetalon"},["q"]="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?"},{["a"]="It is an academic and scientific society of gnomes dedicated to blending the disciplines of arcane magic, alchemical mixtures, and mechanical engineering. Gaxim represents their ideals abroad in Kalimdor.",["al"]={"enlightened assembly","gaxim faction","gaxim group"},["q"]="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?"},{["a"]="Gaxim wants to demonstrate to the night elves that gnomish science and alchemy can actively protect and heal natural woodlands, offering a modern Alliance answer to forest conservation alongside traditional druidism.",["al"]={"why is gaxim here","gaxim night elves","gaxim purpose"},["q"]="Why is Gaxim working with the night elves?"},{["a"]="The Venture Company is ruthlessly clear-cutting Windshear Crag with crude machines and toxic pollution. Gaxim despises their reckless exploitation and relishes turning volatile chemicals and sabotage against their operations.",["al"]={"gaxim venture co","gaxim vs venture company","why fight venture co"},["q"]="Why does Gaxim hate the Venture Company?"},{["a"]="He shares his small outpost with Kaela Shadowspear, a night elf sentinel watching over the trails leading into Windshear Crag.",["al"]={"gaxim companion","who is with gaxim","gaxim and kaela"},["q"]="Who is camped with Gaxim on Webwinder Path?"},{["a"]="He is located at a modest Alliance camp along the Webwinder Path, just southwest of the industrial logging pits of Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.",["al"]={"gaxim location","where is gaxim","gaxim rustfizzle map"},["q"]="Where can Gaxim Rustfizzle be found?"}},["kw"]={"assembly","gaxim","gnome","kaela","rustfizzle","stonetalon","venture company","webwinder","windshear"},["n"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["s"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an ambitious gnome scholar and tinker stationed at a small Alliance camp along the Webwinder Path in Stonetalon Mountains. A representative of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, he seeks to prove to skeptical night elves that advanced artifice and alchemy can preserve their woodland realm. His scientific curiosity is matched by a fierce vendetta against the destructive operations of the Venture Company.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While night elves traditionally rely on ancient druidism and nature magic, Gaxim Rustfizzle arrived in the craggy passes of Stonetalon to demonstrate a radically different perspective. Representing the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences, he genuinely believes that calculated mechanisms and chemical solutions can defend and restore Kalimdor's wilderness just as effectively as prayers to Elune. Camped alongside the sentinel Kaela Shadowspear on the Webwinder Path, he works tirelessly to convince his tall, reclusive allies of engineering's ecological merits.",["t"]="A Scientific Emissary"},{["b"]="Much of Gaxim's energy is channeled against the Venture Company, whose clear-cutting and industrial greed desecrate nearby Windshear Crag. Believing that crude goblin machinery deserves neither respect nor mercy, Gaxim coordinates covert operations and volatile chemical sabotage against their logging operations. To him, crippling their shredders and stealing their schematics is not merely tactical warfare—it is a practical demonstration that superior gnomish intellect always triumphs over careless corporate plunder.",["t"]="Sabotaging the Saws"}}}}}
t["npc:gazrog"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,258,28.475.0,16.330.0,26.129.0,41.187.0,53.196.0,14.237.0,49.145.0,49.211.0",["h"]="cb825d",["n"]="Gazrog",["s"]="Gazrog. Gazrog es un guerrero orco apostado en El Cruce, en el corazón de Los Baldíos. Con la tarea de mantener la logística y la seguridad a lo largo de los peligrosos caminos de la sabana, recluta a viajeros competentes de la Horda para hacer frente a las amenazas regionales e investigar patrullas perdidas. El Cruce sirve como el nudo vital para todo el tránsito de la Horda a través de Kalimdor, pero su aislamiento deja las líneas de suministro vulnerables tanto a merodeadores como a bestias. Gazrog monta guardia junto a los defensores del asentamiento, esforzándose por garantizar que los cargamentos, las monedas y los mensajeros lleguen a sus destinos. Mantener el orden en un territorio tan extenso exige una vigilancia constante, y Gazrog depende enormemente de los aventureros de paso para atajar las crisis que se gestan más allá de las empalizadas del puesto avanzado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Gazrog is an early contact for Horde adventurers leaving Durotar or Mulgore, offering critical work to establish secure travel corridors across Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc veteran holding down the Crossroads, Gazrog embodies the gritty, no-nonsense grit required to tame the unforgiving Kalimdor frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gazrog is located at the Crossroads, the central settlement connecting the northern, southern, and eastern routes of the Barrens.",["al"]={"gazrog location","where is gazrog","gazrog crossroads"},["q"]="Where can Gazrog be found?"},{["a"]="He acts as an operational coordinator and guard at the Crossroads, handing out tasks to safeguard regional supply lines, recover intercepted shipments, and locate missing Horde personnel.",["al"]={"gazrog job","who is gazrog","what does gazrog do"},["q"]="What role does Gazrog play for the Horde?"},{["a"]="Horde coin convoys are frequently targeted by clever savannah raptors and opportunists roaming the Barrens trails, prompting Gazrog to send champions to hunt down the beasts and recover the cargo.",["al"]={"stolen silver quest","who stole the silver","barrens stolen shipment"},["q"]="What happened to the stolen silver Gazrog asks about?"},{["a"]="Dogran is a Horde grunt who was posted to the Crossroads to work with Gazrog. He never returned from duty: Gazrog has heard he is alive but injured and held prisoner by the quilboar, news he would rather keep from Dogran's mate, Zankaja.",["al"]={"news of dogran","where is dogran","gazrog dogran"},["q"]="Who is Dogran?"},{["a"]="No. Gazrog serves the Horde directly out of the Crossroads, maintaining security for orc, tauren, and troll interests across the central Barrens.",["al"]={"is gazrog ratchet","gazrog faction","gazrog goblin"},["q"]="Is Gazrog affiliated with Ratchet or the goblins?"},{["a"]="No one is quite sure. The raptors hid the stolen silver at their nests in the Raptor Grounds south of Ratchet, and Gazrog wonders whether the stories of their intelligence are closer to the mark than he thought.",["al"]={"raptor thieves why","do raptors steal things","raptors shiny"},["q"]="Why are raptors stealing supplies in the Barrens?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","dogran","gazrog","horde outpost","raptor thieves","stolen silver"},["n"]="Gazrog",["s"]="Gazrog is an orc warrior stationed at the Crossroads in the heart of the Barrens. Tasked with maintaining logistics and security along the savannah's perilous roads, he recruits able Horde travelers to deal with regional threats and investigate lost patrols.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Crossroads serves as the vital junction for all Horde transit through Kalimdor, but its isolation leaves supply lines vulnerable to marauders and beasts alike. Gazrog stands watch alongside the settlement's defenders, working to ensure that cargo, coin, and couriers reach their destinations. Maintaining order in a sprawling wilderness requires constant vigilance, and Gazrog relies heavily on passing adventurers to handle crises brewing beyond the outpost's stockades.",["t"]="A Sentinel of the Crossroads"},{["b"]="Between predatory raptors harassing trails and aggressive quillboar clans ambushing scouts, Gazrog's duties never end. He frequently coordinates responses to highway robberies—such as retrieving stolen Horde shipments—and keeps track of missing soldiers like the grunt Dogran, who ended up an injured prisoner of the quilboar.",["t"]="Savannah Hazards"}}}}}
t["npc:gelbin-mekkatorque"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,326,35.716.0,31.706.1,26.203.0,54.282.0,42.264.0,56.249.0,30.191.0",["h"]="8d5f67",["n"]="Gelbin Mekkatorque",["s"]="Gelbin Mekkatorque. Gelbin Mekkatorque es el Manitas Mayor de los gnomos y reside actualmente exiliado en la Ciudad Manitas, dentro de Forjaz. Reconocido como un ingeniero visionario cuyas invenciones incluyen el mecanozancudo y el Tren subterráneo, ahora carga con el pesado fardo de la caída de Gnomeregan y supervisa los esfuerzos para recuperar el hogar ancestral de su pueblo. El liderazgo de los gnomos se gana mediante el intelecto y el mérito en lugar de linajes sanguíneos, y el ascenso de Gelbin Mekkatorque a Manitas Mayor fue impulsado por puro genio inventivo. Graduado en Gearshaft University, Mekkatorque revolucionó el transporte personal con la creación del primer mecanozancudo funcional. A lo largo de décadas de innovación, diseñó el microajustador giromático, robots de reparación automatizados y se asoció con los enanos Barbabronce para diseñar sus formidables máquinas de asedio. Cuando Ventormenta necesitó una conexión de tránsito rápido con Forjaz tras la Segunda Guerra, el Rey Magni Barbabronce recurrió a Mekkatorque, quien dibujó personalmente los esquemas y supervisó la construcción del Tren subterráneo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="Standing before the High Tinker is standing before the author of the mechanostrider, the gyromatic micro-adjustor, and the Deeprun Tram. His workshop in Tinker Town represents the cutting edge of technological innovation.",["race:Gnome"]="Mekkatorque is the heart of your people in exile. Though the guilt of Gnomeregan's poisoning weighs on him, his brilliance and devotion to liberating your ancestral home command absolute loyalty in Tinker Town."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gelbin Mekkatorque is the elected High Tinker and leader of the gnomes. He is a master engineer who designed pivotal gnomish technologies, including the mechanostrider, repair bots, and the Deeprun Tram.",["al"]={"high tinker","gnome leader","who is the gnome king"},["q"]="Who is Gelbin Mekkatorque?"},{["a"]="Gnomeregan was overrun by a savage trogg invasion followed by a catastrophic radioactive fallout. Mekkatorque led the evacuation of his people across Dun Morogh to Ironforge, where King Magni Bronzebeard granted them refuge in Tinker Town while plans are made to take the city back.",["al"]={"why is mekkatorque in ironforge","why are gnomes in ironforge","gnomeregan fall"},["q"]="Why is Mekkatorque in Ironforge instead of Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="Facing endless waves of troggs, Mekkatorque was persuaded by a trusted advisor to vent toxic radioactive coolant into the lower chambers to halt the beasts. Tragically, the gas failed to stop the troggs and instead irradiated the city, killing thousands of gnomes.",["al"]={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan irradiated","thermaplugg betrayal"},["q"]="What caused the catastrophe in Gnomeregan?"},{["a"]="Mekkatorque invented the mechanostrider, giving gnomes their own agile mount. He also designed the gyromatic micro-adjustor, repair bots, the schematics for the Deeprun Tram between Ironforge and Stormwind, and co-developed the dwarven siege engine.",["al"]={"mekkatorque inventions","what did gelbin build"},["q"]="What did Mekkatorque invent before becoming High Tinker?"},{["a"]="Gnomes do not have a hereditary monarchy; their leader is an elected High Tinker chosen on merit and intellectual achievement. His title and authority derive from his election as High Tinker.",["al"]={"is mekkatorque a king","king of gnomes"},["q"]="Is Mekkatorque an actual king?"}},["kw"]={"deeprun tram","gelbin","gnome","gnomeregan","high tinker","ironforge","mechanostrider","mekkatorque","thermaplugg","tinker town"},["n"]="Gelbin Mekkatorque",["s"]="Gelbin Mekkatorque is the High Tinker of the gnomes, currently residing in exile in Tinker Town within Ironforge. Renowned as a visionary engineer whose inventions include the mechanostrider and the Deeprun Tram, he now carries the heavy burden of Gnomeregan's fall and oversees efforts to reclaim his people's ancestral home.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Gnomish leadership is earned through intellect and merit rather than bloodlines, and Gelbin Mekkatorque's rise to High Tinker was propelled by pure inventive genius. A graduate of Gearshaft University, Mekkatorque revolutionized personal transportation with the creation of the first functioning mechanostrider. Over decades of innovation, he drafted the gyromatic micro-adjustor, automated repair bots, and partnered with the Bronzebeard dwarves to engineer their formidable siege engines. When Stormwind required a rapid transit connection to Ironforge after the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard turned to Mekkatorque, who personally drew the schematics and oversaw construction of the subterranean Deeprun Tram.",["t"]="The High Tinker and Master Inventor"},{["b"]="Mekkatorque's greatest tragedy struck when troggs invaded Gnomeregan from deep below. Urged by his trusted friend and chief advisor, Sicco Thermaplugg, Mekkatorque ordered the venting of radioactive waste into the lower corridors to exterminate the attackers. Instead, the toxic gas slaughtered thousands of innocent gnomes and mutated the survivors, while Thermaplugg seized the ruined city. Crushed by guilt yet determined to fix his mistake, Mekkatorque led the surviving refugees across Dun Morogh to Ironforge. Operating out of Tinker Town under King Magni's hospitality, the High Tinker directs gnomekind's military and scientific energies toward a single unwavering objective: liberating Gnomeregan.",["t"]="Betrayal and Exile in Ironforge"}}}}}
t["npc:gelihast"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,284,16.355.0,24.334.0,16.204.0,41.193.0,43.217.0,34.177.0,35.104.0,49.163.0",["h"]="7b8ca2",["n"]="Gelihast",["s"]="Gelihast. Gelihast es un feroz líder múrloc que empuña dos espadas y reside en Alberca de Ask'ar, en las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Atraído por los oscuros susurros de los Dioses Antiguos, se abrió paso masacrando hasta las ruinas del templo sumergido antes de ganarse el reacio respeto de los cultores del Martillo Crepuscular. Mientras que la mayoría de los múrlocs permanecen cerca de los bajíos costeros, Gelihast sintió la oscura y ominosa atracción de los Dioses Antiguos en las profundidades de Vallefresno. Impulsado por estos susurros primordiales, se abrió camino por la fuerza hasta el templo sumergido de las Cavernas de Brazanegra. Cuando los cultores del Martillo Crepuscular intentaron cerrarle el paso, mató él solo a casi una docena de ellos usando sus espadas dobles.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Gelihast attacks with blinding sword speed; skilled warriors who brace themselves can turn his frantic dual-wielding assault entirely against him.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces seeking to cleanse the corruption leaking into Ashenvale, removing Gelihast is essential to secure the northern passages of the submerged temple.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers dispatched to scour Blackfathom Deeps must eliminate Gelihast to disrupt the cultist alliance festering beneath the Zoram Strand."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gelihast is a vicious murloc chieftain who commands the Blindlight tribe inside the Pool of Ask'ar in Blackfathom Deeps. He fights with twin blades and serves the dark presence lingering within the ruins.",["al"]={"who is gelihast","gelihast lore","gelihast background"},["q"]="Who is Gelihast?"},{["a"]="He was drawn by the whispers of the Old Gods. Desiring to reach the source of the dark call, he invaded the ruins and carved a bloody path through the local cultists to claim his own territory.",["al"]={"why is there a murloc in bfd","why is gelihast in the temple"},["q"]="Why is Gelihast inside Blackfathom Deeps?"},{["a"]="Although Gelihast slaughtered nearly a dozen Twilight's Hammer cultists upon entering the temple, the survivors were so impressed by his ferocity and cruelty that they permitted him to stay and worship alongside them.",["al"]={"gelihast and twilights hammer","do cultists like gelihast"},["q"]="How did the Twilight's Hammer react to him?"},{["a"]="Gelihast erected the shrine to offer bloody sacrifices to the ominous presence in the ruins. Travelers who defeat him can touch the altar to receive the Blessing of Blackfathom.",["al"]={"altar of the deep","gelihast altar","blessing of blackfathom altar"},["q"]="What is the altar behind Gelihast?"},{["a"]="He leads the Blindlight murlocs, an aggressive tribe that infests the Pool of Ask'ar within the caverns.",["al"]={"gelihast tribe","what murlocs are in bfd"},["q"]="What tribe of murlocs does he lead?"},{["a"]="He continues to sacrifice victims at his altar in the Pool of Ask'ar, serving as a vicious enforcer and fanatic servant of the shadowy horrors infesting the ruins.",["al"]={"gelihast fate","who kills gelihast"},["q"]="What happens to Gelihast if he is left unchecked?"}},["kw"]={"blackfathom deeps","blindlight","gelihast","murloc","old gods","pool of ask'ar","twilight's hammer"},["n"]="Gelihast",["s"]="Gelihast is a ferocious, twin-blade wielding murloc chieftain residing in the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps. Lured by the dark whispers of the Old Gods, he butchered his way into the sunken temple ruins before earning the reluctant respect of the Twilight's Hammer cultists.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While most murlocs stay near coastal shallows, Gelihast felt the dark, ominous tug of the Old Gods deep beneath Ashenvale. Driven by these primordial whispers, he forced his way into the sunken temple of Blackfathom Deeps. When Twilight's Hammer cultists tried to halt his path, he slaughtered nearly a dozen of them single-handedly using his twin swords.",["t"]="A Deadly Calling"},{["b"]="Rather than seeking vengeance, the cultists admired Gelihast's raw savagery and granted him dominion over the Pool of Ask'ar. There, surrounded by his Blindlight brood, the bloodthirsty murloc constructed a crude altar. He performs grim sacrifices upon it, receiving dark boons directly from the foul presence slumbering in the abyss.",["t"]="Master of the Blindlight"}}}}}
t["npc:ghamoo-ra-classic"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,251,24.464.0,21.379.0,17.233.0,38.222.0,28.87.0,27.161.0,45.220.0",["h"]="e9fcfc",["n"]="Ghamoo-ra",["s"]="Ghamoo-ra. Ghamoo-ra es una antigua tortuga marina gigante que habita en Alberca de Ask'ar, dentro de Cavernas de Brazanegra. Antaño un habitante pacífico del templo sumergido de Elune, fue capturado, torturado y conducido a la locura por el culto del Martillo Crepuscular para servir como un feroz guardián. Antes de la profanación de Cavernas de Brazanegra, Ghamoo-ra se contaba entre los últimos habitantes naturales y pacíficos que moraban entre las ruinas anegadas del templo de los elfos de la noche dedicado a Elune. Cuando el nihilista culto del Martillo Crepuscular tomó el control del santuario, arrancó a la antigua tortuga de su vida tranquila y la encerró en cautiverio. En lugar de matarla, la atormentaron sistemáticamente durante años, sometiéndola a un desollamiento físico y mental a manos de los miembros del culto.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids view Ghamoo-ra's torment and forced aggression as a tragic corruption of natural wildlife by the servants of the Old Gods.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters venturing into Blackfathom Deeps may pity Ghamoo-ra, a noble, ancient beast broken by dark captivity, though a patient hunter may yet tame him.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Ghamoo-ra's plight is a bitter reminder of the defilement of Elune's sacred temple by the vile Twilight's Hammer."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ghamoo-ra is a giant turtle found in the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps. Originally a peaceful dweller of the temple of Elune, he was captured, tortured, and broken into a ferocious guard beast by the Twilight's Hammer cult.",["al"]={"ghamoo-ra lore","giant turtle bfd","who is ghamoo ra"},["q"]="Who is Ghamoo-ra?"},{["a"]="The Twilight's Hammer cult imprisoned the turtle and tortured him over several years, breaking his spirit and driving him to utter madness. They conditioned him to lash out at any outsider who approaches the inner shrines.",["al"]={"why is turtle angry","why does turtle attack","ghamoo-ra madness"},["q"]="Why is Ghamoo-ra hostile to outsiders?"},{["a"]="Yes. Despite his size and years of torment, Ghamoo-ra can be tamed by a skilled hunter.",["al"]={"tame ghamoo-ra","can hunter tame bfd turtle"},["q"]="Can a hunter tame Ghamoo-ra?"},{["a"]="The Pool of Ask'ar is a flooded subterranean cavern in Blackfathom Deeps. Ghamoo-ra roams the center of a small island there, encircled by docile native turtles.",["al"]={"pool of ask'ar","where is ghamoo ra"},["q"]="What is the Pool of Ask'ar?"},{["a"]="While not inherently a creature of the Void, Ghamoo-ra's mind was warped by Twilight's Hammer cultists who worship the Old Gods. They twisted the ancient creature into an unwitting protector of their dark ritual grounds.",["al"]={"ghamoo-ra old gods","is turtle corrupted"},["q"]="What connection does he have to the Old Gods?"}},["kw"]={"blackfathom deeps","elune","ghamoo-ra","pool of ask'ar","tame","turtle","twilight's hammer"},["n"]="Ghamoo-ra",["s"]="Ghamoo-ra is an ancient, giant sea turtle inhabiting the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps. Once a peaceful denizen of Elune's sunken temple, he was captured, tortured, and driven mad by the Twilight's Hammer cult to serve as a vicious guardian.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the defilement of Blackfathom Deeps, Ghamoo-ra was among the last peaceful natural inhabitants dwelling among the flooded ruins of the night elven temple dedicated to Elune. When the nihilistic Twilight's Hammer cult took control of the sanctuary, they roused the ancient turtle from his quiet life and locked him in captivity. Rather than slain, he was systematically tormented for years, suffering mental and physical flaying at the hands of the cultists.",["t"]="A Gentle Beast Tormented"},{["b"]="Broken by prolonged cruelty, the great turtle finally succumbed to madness. Bestowing the name Ghamoo-ra upon the ruined creature, the cultists trained him into a ferocious defense beast. Now patrolling a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar surrounded by lesser turtles, Ghamoo-ra blindly attacks any intruders who enter the caverns, serving the very cult that shattered his mind.",["t"]="Guardian of the Deeps"}}}}}
t["npc:gilnid"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,339,21.433.0,21.374.1,14.208.0,31.218.0,26.155.0,28.179.0,45.177.0,41.182.0",["h"]="c4da8c",["n"]="Gilnid",["s"]="Gilnid. Gilnid, conocido como el Fundidor, es el maestro ingeniero goblin que dirige las forjas en las profundidades de Las Minas de la Muerte. Supervisa la fundición del mineral en bruto para transformarlo en metal refinado y munición para el acorazado secreto de Edwin VanCleef. Sin sus ardientes operaciones, la Hermandad Defias carecería de los cañones pesados necesarios para asaltar Ventormenta. En lo profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte, la Hermandad Defias recurre a la pericia industrial para forjar armas de guerra. Gilnid ejerce como jefe de fundición de VanCleef y comanda un pequeño ejército de peones, manitas y herreros goblin en la fundición central. Al ser más corpulento que la mayoría de los suyos, somete a su cuadrilla a un ritmo implacable entre humo y escoria, ladrando órdenes y negándoles descansos para garantizar que el mineral de hierro en bruto se transforme en pesados blindajes y munición letal.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Stopping Gilnid shuts down the Defias weapons assembly line, preventing VanCleef's warship from being fully armed before it can threaten Stormwind Harbor.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gilnid's foundry is a prime example of goblin heavy industry, churning out standardized naval cannons, ammunition, and structural plating under extreme conditions.",["profession:Mining"]="The massive blast furnaces and smelting pots in Gilnid's workshop demonstrate how the Defias Brotherhood turns the raw mineral wealth of Westfall into refined iron and armaments."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gilnid is a goblin engineer and the head smelter for Edwin VanCleef in the Deadmines. He oversees the Brotherhood's forges and leads the industrial effort to cast cannons and ammunition for their war machine.",["al"]={"gilnid deadmines","who is gilnid","the smelter"},["q"]="Who is Gilnid?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood hired mercenary goblin engineers to build and supply their hidden warship. Gilnid was placed in charge of the smelting works, transforming mined iron ore into refined parts, armor, and artillery.",["al"]={"why is a goblin in deadmines","gilnid defias lore","what is gilnid doing"},["q"]="Why is Gilnid in the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="Gilnid is responsible for manufacturing the massive cannons, ship parts, and shot needed to arm the juggernaut hidden in the docks deeper inside the mines.",["al"]={"gilnid cannon","what is gilnid building","deadmines forge purpose"},["q"]="What is Gilnid working on?"},{["a"]="Gilnid controls the industrial foundry blocking the path to the cove. The heavy blast doors leading deeper toward the Defias ship remain sealed until the smelting room is secured.",["al"]={"why kill gilnid","door past gilnid"},["q"]="Why must Gilnid be defeated?"},{["a"]="Yes. He is not a member of the original Stonemasons, but rather a contracted goblin specialist serving directly under VanCleef to handle heavy metallurgy and weapons production.",["al"]={"vancleef and gilnid","is gilnid defias leader"},["q"]="Does Gilnid work directly for Edwin VanCleef?"},{["a"]="Gilnid leads a specialized goblin engineering crew in the foundry. They operate the blast furnaces, pour molten iron, and assemble ordnance under his strict, unrelenting supervision.",["al"]={"gilnid goblins","deadmines forge crew"},["q"]="Why are there so many goblins around him?"}},["kw"]={"cannons","deadmines","defias","forge","foundry","gilnid","goblin","juggernaut","smelter","vancleef"},["n"]="Gilnid",["s"]="Gilnid, known as the Smelter, is the goblin master engineer running the forges in the depths of the Deadmines. He oversees the smelting of raw ore into refined metal and munitions for Edwin VanCleef's hidden ironclad juggernaut. Without his fiery operations, the Defias Brotherhood would lack the heavy cannons needed to assault Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Deep within the Deadmines, the Defias Brotherhood relies on industrial expertise to forge weapons of war. Gilnid serves as VanCleef's head smelter, commanding a small army of goblin laborers, tinkers, and smiths in the central foundry. Towering over most of his kin, he drives his crew relentlessly through smoke and slag, barking orders and refusing breaks to ensure raw iron ore is processed into heavy plating and lethal ordnance.",["t"]="Master of the Foundry"},{["b"]="The smelting works are critical to the Brotherhood's grand ambition. Gilnid is directly responsible for forging the heavy cannons and ammunition intended for the colossal ironclad warship docked in the subterranean cove beyond his workshop. Until his foundry churns out every gun, barrel, and ball, the Defias vessel remains unready for its planned strike against Stormwind.",["t"]="Arming the Juggernaut"}}}}}
t["npc:glorin-steelbrow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,405,19.496.0,32.444.1,24.239.0,34.128.0,57.294.0,48.240.0,26.243.0,33.221.0",["h"]="25342b",["n"]="Glorin Frenteacerada",["s"]="Glorin Frenteacerada. Glorin Frenteacerada es un agente enano al que se puede encontrar bebiendo en el Mesón Aguahonda, en Puerto de Menethil. Como colaborador del Obispo Lontananza, de la Catedral de la Luz en Ventormenta, ayuda a los aventureros a investigar la desaparecida Tercera Flota y a recuperar reliquias y materiales sagrados dispersos por la costa de Los Humedales. Sus esfuerzos conectan directamente las tierras embrujadas de Bosque del Ocaso con los pecios sumergidos del norte. Mientras el Obispo Lontananza ayuda a los habitantes de Bosque del Ocaso contra sus terrores acechantes desde la Catedral de la Luz en Ventormenta, mantiene contactos muy al norte, en Puerto de Menethil. Apostado en el bullicioso Mesón Aguahonda, Glorin Frenteacerada actúa como los ojos y las manos de Lontananza en la costa. Ofrece ayuda y orientación a los viajeros enviados al norte en busca de metales sagrados y reliquias olvidadas, sirviendo de puente crucial entre los problemas del bosque del sur y los restos hundidos de Los Humedales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Paladins following Farthing's orders will find Glorin indispensable in recovering Lightforge iron, a sacred metal essential for crafting weapons blessed by the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="Glorin plays a key role in recovering crucial Alliance military relics and sanctified materials lost during naval disasters in the Wetlands.",["race:Dwarf"]="Glorin represents dwarven enterprise and solidarity, coordinating from the maritime hub of Menethil Harbor to support allies across Khaz Modan and the southern human kingdoms."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarf stationed in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. He works in coordination with Bishop Farthing of Stormwind, assisting adventurers who travel north to salvage sunken cargo and relics off the Wetlands coast.",["al"]={"who is glorin","glorin steelbrow lore","what does glorin do"},["q"]="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?"},{["a"]="Glorin is located on the ground floor of the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, situated on the western coast of the Wetlands.",["al"]={"glorin location","where is glorin steelbrow","glorin deepwater tavern"},["q"]="Where can I find Glorin Steelbrow?"},{["a"]="Bishop Farthing of Stormwind's Cathedral of Light seeks powerful holy relics and consecrated metals to fight the darkness encroaching on Duskwood. He sends trusted emissaries to Glorin Steelbrow, who knows the Wetlands coast and can point salvagers toward the sunken remains of the Third Fleet.",["al"]={"why duskwood quest in wetlands","connection to farthing","why send to wetlands"},["q"]="Why is a dwarf in Menethil Harbor involved with Duskwood?"},{["a"]="The Third Fleet was an Alliance naval expedition that met catastrophe off the coast of the Wetlands. Its shattered hulls now litter the seabed, haunted by drowned sailors and hiding valuable cargo like Lightforge iron and ancient artifacts.",["al"]={"what is the doomed fleet","third fleet wetlands","the doomed fleet quest"},["q"]="What is the Third Fleet that Glorin talks about?"},{["a"]="The Eye of Paleth is an ancient religious relic carried aboard the sunken fleet. Once recovered from the ocean floor with Glorin's guidance, it must undergo cleansing by the priesthood due to the dark corruption lingering around the shipwreck.",["al"]={"eye of paleth","paleth relic","what is eye of paleth"},["q"]="What is the Eye of Paleth?"},{["a"]="Lightforge iron is a rare, sanctified metal used to craft blessed weapons capable of striking down powerful undead and demonic forces. Glorin helps recover lost ingots from the shipwrecks to aid the defenders of Duskwood.",["al"]={"lightforge iron","lost ingots","blessed arm"},["q"]="What is Lightforge iron used for?"}},["kw"]={"bishop farthing","deepwater tavern","doomed fleet","duskwood","eye of paleth","glorin steelbrow","lightforge iron","menethil harbor","wetlands"},["n"]="Glorin Steelbrow",["s"]="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven operative found drinking at the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Acting as an associate of Bishop Farthing of Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, he helps adventurers investigate the lost Third Fleet and recover sacred relics and materials scattered across the Wetlands coast. His efforts tie the haunted wilderness of Duskwood directly to the sunken shipwrecks of the north.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Bishop Farthing aids the people of Duskwood against its creeping terrors from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light, he maintains ties far to the north in Menethil Harbor. Stationed inside the bustling Deepwater Tavern, Glorin Steelbrow acts as Farthing's eyes and hands on the coast. He offers aid and direction to travelers sent north in search of sacred metals and forgotten relics, providing a crucial bridge between the troubles of the southern forest and the sunken wreckage of the Wetlands.",["t"]="A Harbor Connection"},{["b"]="Steelbrow is intimately familiar with the tragedy of the Third Fleet, whose ships were battered and dragged beneath the waves along the Wetlands shore. He guides adventurers to scour the haunted wreckage for lost ingots of Lightforge iron and the powerful, cursed artifact known as the Eye of Paleth. Glorin knows that recovering such holy armaments is vital for forging weapons capable of holding back the dark forces threatening the Alliance.",["t"]="The Doomed Fleet and Lost Relics"}}}}}
